{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/393536-inferno-2nd-edition","id":393536,"title":"Inferno: 2nd Edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-05T02:13:17-08:00","id":393536,"title":"Inferno: 2nd Edition","content":"Now, while it is unlikely to come to pass, let us say there was talk about updating the Inferno book to Second Edition. Yay or nay? Do you think Inferno needs an update? If so, what would you like to see and what would you like changed from the first book? We're already talking Second Sight, so let's give demons some love too, eh?<br /> <br /> Personally, I would love to see more details on the L'enfant Diabolique, which is a concept I see a lot of potential in that was sadly untapped. Maybe not as playable characters but more mechanics and fluff on how they work. Is evil really natural to them, what is their role in cults? Do they actively work with or for Infernal demons, or do they primarily do their own thing? How does the creation of one of these beings even happen when demons are intangible creatures without the potential to produce offspring with most not-Twilight creatures? I really like the idea and would like to see more of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4906-deraneo","name":"Deraneo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T02:25:01-08:00","id":393553,"title":"","content":"Definitely yay. Inferno was one of my personal favourites books of previous-nWoD. I'd like to see development in the Empyrean area, as i think the definition of Virtue-specific spirits is still left somewhat vague... and could be as awesome as the description of the Demons that Inferno settled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T03:52:32-08:00","id":393635,"title":"","content":"Inferno, to me, is heavily tied to the Hunter gameline. I personally say that it should be included in the Hunter 2e book first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T04:13:51-08:00","id":393642,"title":"","content":"That's a book that definitely needs update to second edition(along with Second Sight, Innocents, Skinchangers and Immortals in that order for me)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T05:09:14-08:00","id":393656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/393536-inferno-2nd-edition?p=393635#post393635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Inferno, to me, is heavily tied to the Hunter gameline. I personally say that it should be included in the Hunter 2e book first.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> While heavily tied, I'd still consider it purely a blue supplement. Let's not exclude the average mortals and the rest of gamelines out of the Inferno fun <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> For example, I won't be getting Hunter books... but a blue book about inferno - that's a different matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T06:04:17-08:00","id":393674,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't like to see as much a remake of Inferno, as just additional material for it. When you consider how much Demons, sin and vice are brought up in WoD, its sorta funny that the actual forceses of Hell are relegated to a single blue book supplement. I love the book Inferno to death, especially the extrapolated &quot;Hell Vs Heaven&quot; you can create fairly effectively with the Empyriean Page and Hunters, but I'm afraid that a new rendition of it, would be overshadowed by the entire &quot;God-Machine/Mechanical Demons&quot;. If a new rendition was to be made, it would be important to somehow clarify that that games setting is entirely seperate from that of the God-Machine, which I think would be difficult to pull off. I have faith that if the writers decide to attempt it, that they'll do a good job, but I would saddened to see the Inferno setting smothered by the God-Machine and its interpritation of Demons. Dont get me wrong, I think the God-Machine and its bio-mechanical Demons are immensely awesome, but I wouldn't like them to gobble up the setting and themes of Inferno.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T06:56:25-08:00","id":393713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/393536-inferno-2nd-edition?p=393674#post393674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't like to see as much a remake of Inferno, as just additional material for it. When you consider how much Demons, sin and vice are brought up in WoD, its sorta funny that the actual forceses of Hell are relegated to a single blue book supplement. I love the book Inferno to death, especially the extrapolated &quot;Hell Vs Heaven&quot; you can create fairly effectively with the Empyriean Page and Hunters, but I'm afraid that a new rendition of it, would be overshadowed by the entire &quot;God-Machine/Mechanical Demons&quot;. If a new rendition was to be made, it would be important to somehow clarify that that games setting is entirely seperate from that of the God-Machine, which I think would be difficult to pull off. I have faith that if the writers decide to attempt it, that they'll do a good job, but I would saddened to see the Inferno setting smothered by the God-Machine and its interpritation of Demons. Dont get me wrong, I think the God-Machine and its bio-mechanical Demons are immensely awesome, but I wouldn't like them to gobble up the setting and themes of Inferno.</div> </div> </div> </div>considering all the wordcount they used again and again in order to clarify that Inferno's demons are separate thing from the Descent ones, I don't think that in the theoretical case they'll give Inferno a second addition they would just through everything away and say &quot;so now they are the same! now, lets make Geist into spirit claimed and be absorbed into Werewolf!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T07:02:05-08:00","id":393717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/393536-inferno-2nd-edition?p=393713#post393713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> considering all the wordcount they used again and again in order to clarify that Inferno's demons are separate thing from the Descent ones, I don't think that in the theoretical case they'll give Inferno a second addition they would just through everything away and say &quot;so now they are the same! now, lets make Geist into spirit claimed and be absorbed into Werewolf!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I know. As I mentioned, I am hardly afraid that they'll make them precisely the same thing, but rather afraid that the idea of the unopposable and uncompromising power of Hell and/or Empyriean, will be dimminnished by the neigh omnipotent the God-Machine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T07:34:38-08:00","id":393731,"title":"","content":"amm... I don't know if you noticed, but last time I've checked there are a number of &quot;omnipotent&quot; forces in WoD beside the God Machine- the Principle, the Wyrd, Fate, the Devourer and the Supernal to name a few. Adding the Devil and/or God to the mix won't change much. This is why the &quot;canon&quot; view is that the God Machine is as powerful as you want it to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T08:02:11-08:00","id":393739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/393536-inferno-2nd-edition?p=393731#post393731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">amm... I don't know if you noticed, but last time I've checked there are a number of &quot;omnipotent&quot; forces in WoD beside the God Machine- the Principle, the Wyrd, Fate, the Devourer and the Supernal to name a few. Adding the Devil and/or God to the mix won't change much. This is why the &quot;canon&quot; view is that the God Machine is as powerful as you want it to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, lets try to be polite here.<br /> Secondly, yes, the Principle, the Wyrd, Fate and the Supernal are power forceses of nature, but therein lies the rub. They are forces of nature, like gravity. Its not like Fate or the Supernal will send an avatar of itself, to kick your ass because you fucked with its timeshare. The Principle might do that, but its just as likely to send an avatar of itself to bless you with divine strenght and good fortune because you fucked with said timeshare. Though it does have agents, they are as much a conundrum as the Principle itself, which remains incredibly vaguely defined.<br /> I dont know what &quot;The Devourer&quot; is, so I cant comment on that.<br /> <br /> None of the ones I commented on are as clearly defined and &quot;in your face&quot; as the God-Machine. The merest existance of them are a question not without its merit, whereas the God-Machine is visibly and tangibly real and out to get you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T08:19:08-08:00","id":393749,"title":"","content":"The thing with Inferno was that the possessed actually gelled really well with the old, buggy morality system. They've got an alien presence in their head dragging them down to commit atrocities and driving them nuts while it was at it. Plus the whole sin theme. Integrity just doesn't feel as right with the system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T08:49:40-08:00","id":393785,"title":"","content":"As one o more avid STs to run Maeljin's of <b>Werewolf</b> as a Demon Princesses of <b>Inferno</b> I will tell something from our game playtests.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/393536-inferno-2nd-edition?p=393749#post393749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing with Inferno was that the possessed actually gelled really well with the old, buggy morality system. They've got an alien presence in their head dragging them down to commit atrocities and driving them nuts while it was at it. Plus the whole sin theme. Integrity just doesn't feel as right with the system.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not see this a problem. In 1ed Morality you had a <b>outside</b> sins - rigid structures you need to adhere. In 2ed Integrity rules you have <b>your own</b> sins - things that are destroying your inner &quot;stability&quot;. But they are both <i>sins</i>. They are still about transgression. And this turmoil characters are receiving from lowering Integrity, demons of Inferno can use to make stronger impact on the Possessed. Think about it - who is more easier to control in mortal realm - man that is doing many bad things from the outside point ( 1ed low Moerality ), or the man that has lost his inner compass and is <b><i>unstable</i></b> emotional ( 2ed low Integrity )? I would put my money on the second option as the Demon Lord. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The problem of 2ed rules for the Inferno is that Virtue and Vice are now open, so anyone can choose anything they think is their &quot;good&quot; and &quot;bad&quot; side. But taking really a look on the sheet and think for 5 minutes will lend you answers. By the example from <b>GMC</b>, character with Vice of Ambitious, is, in reality, working for the Pride Great Sin. It does not matter he thinks he is not egocentric - he's &quot;ambition to the death ( his or his close ones )&quot; is Pride in other disguise. The <b>Inferno</b> book would say it's just different Malepraxis. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Second, as to the &quot;God Machine vs Inferno&quot; problem, I resolved this long ago, in my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/213767-more-classical-demons-and-angels-setting-hack\">DtD setting shard</a>. We can have two ( or even more ) forces that use angelo- and demonology imaginary in various lines - becuase the nWoD is created on assumption of Great Mystery of the settings. I even see very much the positives of this kind marriage - it's the most crossover-friendly stuff in all the lines. All we need in <b>Inferno</b> 2ed to have two new Agendas for Unchained for Inferno and Empyrean support, and we are golden. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-05-2015, 11:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T10:45:09-08:00","id":393939,"title":"","content":"The multiple demon types thing was never a problem because nwod already had about 3 sorts anyway. Same with angels.<br /> <br /> Old style Virtue and Vice could just make a comeback for the possessed in the same way that Vamps replace them with Mask and Dirge.<br /> <br /> Maybe just Vice for demons and just Virtue for angels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T10:50:54-08:00","id":393971,"title":"","content":"We've had a thread about this before, I'd link it but I don't want to look for it.<br /> <br /> You could easily keep the GMC Vice and Virtue system, especially if you went as wyrdhamster says and kept the integrity system, which instead of allowing moral cracks to let the demons in, allows other cracks to do the same. With Vice and Virtue it is, each deimply end up with more demons. As it is, each demon has a malpraxis, a vice and a thing. Moving away their vices from the Seven Sins simply allows for more demons, urging you to give into that vice to extreme degrees, or in situations where you shouldn't, or corrupting it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T10:55:17-08:00","id":393973,"title":"","content":"Actually thinking about it it does let you run angels without awkwardly inverting the mechanics as much. Low-integrity angel possessed who have become obsessed with policing everyone around them, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T11:17:48-08:00","id":393989,"title":"","content":"Inferno was great but had a lot of problems. A 2nd edition would be most welcome; covering possession and infernalism in a more classic take than Demon does. Plus, it could double as an Arkatheroi resource for Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T13:47:58-08:00","id":394089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/393536-inferno-2nd-edition?p=393674#post393674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't like to see as much a remake of Inferno, as just additional material for it. When you consider how much Demons, sin and vice are brought up in WoD, its sorta funny that the actual forceses of Hell are relegated to a single blue book supplement.</div> </div> </div> </div>A 2e revamp (as I currently understand it) would require an overhaul of how the mechanics work.<br /> <br /> 1e works on the standard sin list of Lust, Greed, Envy, etc which ties in perfectly with Inferno.<br /> <br /> 2e vices and virtues are more...nuanced and leaves Inferno's material underlying mechanics completely borked.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T14:19:59-08:00","id":394109,"title":"","content":"Nah, the 7 deadlies just become power categories like arcarna dots are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T14:46:22-08:00","id":394135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/393536-inferno-2nd-edition?p=393973#post393973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually thinking about it it does let you run angels without awkwardly inverting the mechanics as much. Low-integrity angel possessed who have become obsessed with policing everyone around them, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>It also allows you to have &quot;Angels&quot; as Demons with unusual Vices.<br /> <br /> Like a Demon with a Vice of Charity and a Key of The Poor; sounds pretty angelic to me!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T15:00:01-08:00","id":394150,"title":"","content":"Yeah; I could see the \u201cSeven Deadly Sins\u201d thing remain the default organizing principle for Possessed powers, detached from Vices. OTOH, perhaps supplement it with guidelines for constructing your own powers around some other kind of sin, along with a worked example. <br /> <br /> The Infernal and the Unchained should <i>not</i> be conflated. In fact, I\u2019d dearly love to see a section added for how the Infernal and the Unchained interact, written very clearly from the perspective that they\u2019re two different kinds of things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T21:26:13-08:00","id":394429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/393536-inferno-2nd-edition?p=394150#post394150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Infernal and the Unchained should <i>not</i> be conflated. In fact, I\u2019d dearly love to see a section added for how the Infernal and the Unchained interact, written very clearly from the perspective that they\u2019re two different kinds of things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mixed - maybe not. But as I pointed in my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/213767-more-classical-demons-and-angels-setting-hack\">DtD setting shard</a>, I easily could see an Agendas of Unchained working for Inferno ( or Empyrean, the second one ). It would nice alternative to Integrators default obsession with God Machine and lend natural crossover area. Imagine this &quot;theological&quot; disputes of two Unchained from different Agendas, one saying that in God Machine is their place and the other that in Inferno lies literal Hell for them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> On the other hand - I could not see Inferno's demons working for the God Machine beside &quot;it's all the same, in the end&quot;. Well, maybe as Inferno's demon summon ritual goes bad, the nearest ( or best fitting ) Unchained is summoned instead?<br /> <br /> In my shard I point out that God Machine Angels were made as vessels for Inferno and Empyrean powers on beginning of time, but then GM become independent and stared to give them sentient. Maybe something in this vein as standard interaction?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-06-2015, 12:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T21:50:37-08:00","id":394462,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d rather not. Yes, a fan can mix and match elements of the two to create something different from both; but that\u2019s more the purview of a Translation Guide or Mirrors-like book. Inferno 2e should address the Unchained n a manner similar to how it addresses vampires: as a wholly separate kind of entity that mortals often mistake for the Inferno\u2019s demons, with an emphasis on how they interact with each other as written. <br /> <br /> This is largely because the two are based on fundamentally different paradigms. Inferno\u2019s demons are creatures of Vice who subsist on humanity\u2019s corruption, and for whom Hell (that is, the Inferno) is a place they escaped from. If they have any connection or opposition to a higher being, they\u2019re not saying. By contrast, the Unchained are former slaves of the God-Machine who have essentially sided with humanity against its oppressor (often in a \u201cthe enemy of my enemy is my friend\u201d sort of way; but still). For them, Hell represents the goal that they strive <i>toward</i>: a place or state of being where they\u2019re beyond the God-Machine\u2019s reach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T01:59:02-08:00","id":394624,"title":"","content":"Marrying the Inferno with the Demons of the God-Machine is, in my opinion at least, detrimental to the underlying theme and mood of both works. Inferno deals with human evil and perversion manifesting in very literal ways while GMC and Demon the Descent deal with alien forces working through mysterious and esoteric means to facilitate an agenda that is often detrimental to the human condition. Sidebars in Inferno even suggest demons might be born of human nightmare as per the Buddhist thought and the Inferno is simply the conceptual plane they return to. These themes and moods are a very different kind of horror from each other. One is personal, the other alien.<br /> <br /> Simply because both groups are called &quot;demons&quot; and may have relation to something called an &quot;angel&quot; and may dislike someone called &quot;God&quot; doesn't necessitate that they are in anyway related. Otherwise we're going to have to immediately relate back to the Demons, Demons, Demons... sidebar in Demon: the Descent and ask the questions:<br /> <br /> Who begot the Lucifuge? They believe they were created by fallen angels in the Miltonian sense. Are Miltonian demons living in the Inferno? They certainly aren't creatures of Vice.<br /> Are the demons of space and mind found by Mages Inferno demons or belong to the God-Machine? Are the demons that Changelings find in human dreams also Inferno demons?<br /> <br /> Remember also: The God-Machine lies. It may not be anything resembling a real God. It's angels may only be called angels, programmed to refer to themselves as angels, and often use those images simply to impose awe on Mankind through the imitation of something else. More so, then, the Unchained are demons because that helps the God-Machine find them as humanity are predisposed to being in opposition to anything &quot;demonic&quot;. Maybe we, and they, call themselves angels and demons simply because that is the word the God-Machine finds most advantageous to designate them as.<br /> <br /> I think what a lot of folks seem to forget is that &quot;demon&quot; doesn't mean anything, even within the modern consciousness. It means a malignant force or simply a malign presence. Demons in Asian mythology aren't even necessarily evil, some can just be playful or goofy spirits.<br /> <br /> Also, I might be splitting hairs on terminology here, but Western Renaissance depictions of demons are not &quot;Classical&quot;. If anything Demon the Descent and it's Gnostic interpretation of the Angel and Demon as the Archon and Fallen Archon are far more &quot;Classical&quot; as relates to the classical period. Demons as creatures of vice are relatively new in the lifespan of the Western ethical faiths. They require the existence of the Seven Deadly Sins, a concept that didn't enter into Christian thought until at least the year 800, but likely post 1100 as prior to this only the theological virtues were focused on (Love, Hope and Faith).<br /> <br /> I would love to see an update to Inferno that would make them completely discrete beings from the Unchained and remind everyone that we can have more than one thing called a &quot;demon&quot; and more than one thing called an &quot;angel&quot; and they don't need to be related to each other. Koala Bears aren't even bears! (And you should never call them Koala Bears, because they're Koalas, bad. Bad!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T04:32:12-08:00","id":394665,"title":"","content":"I think any game that uses inferno is probably operating under at least the assumption that the seven deadly sins entered Christian thought <i>because</i> they are categories of demonic malapraxis. Like &quot;there are these horrible things that feed on negative human behaviour, and they fall into these seven types...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T07:03:04-08:00","id":394746,"title":"","content":"I really think that the first thing that needs to happen, before any attempt at any kind of conversion can be made, is some kind of consensus on what Inferno is wanted for. The inferno is also a mix of all sorts of evil beings from all sorts of mythos and stories, and none of them at all. While the whole Christian-style demons is one possible story, it is far and away from the definitive story. As such, there is no real reason for keeping the Seven Sins. They were used in the past because they were the seven vices the WoD game used - it was a hard coded aspect of the WoD. Now, its not, and forcing the Infernal demons to conform to them when they are supposed to represent evil ephemeral beings of all sorts? It feels very much forced, an attempt to shoe horn something into a Christian cultural imperialistic mold. And, frankly speaking, its not needed. There's no point to it, other than forcing a way to make the current mechanics for the Possessed work- not needed, when we could do so many other ways of buying powers.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyways, circling back to the whole &quot;what do people want this for?&quot; I still feel like its just another WoD book in the same vein as Book of Spirits and Book of the Dead. All three of the books (four if you count the GMC as &quot;angels for mortals&quot;) are designed for dealing with the Shadow and Underworld for the average person. This one was designed for &quot;dealing with infernal demons for mortals.&quot;<br /> <br /> What do people want it for? Playing as a Christian-style demon is already covered through Demon: the Descent. Yes, I know that some people disagree with that statement, but that argument is moot for a simple reason - Onyx Path goes out of its way to make sure the games are remarkably distinct. The chances of another game that uses the &quot;Fallen being against a higher Creator&quot; line is very slim, no matter your view of Descent.<br /> <br /> So, what is it? Is it just for playing a Lucifuge style character, a person torn by a large natural inclination (and capacity) to do (and command) evil, with the desire to do good? I know there have been many who've stated that the Lucifuge would make an awesome stand-alone game in the past. Is this an extension of that?<br /> <br /> You can't have a 2e version of the Inferno without answering that question. What purpose would it serve that a simple rule update couldn't? Inferno doesn't use the seven sins, but any vice. If anything, Inferno demons feeding on rotting Integrity &quot;evils&quot; is a better fit for the book than Morality was. Done with chapter 1 update. Chapter 2's update would involve changing the powers, but the pact mechanics itself is fine. Sample demons? Again, just updating powers. L'Enfant Diablique? They're literally evil Lucifuge, tied into Hunter. A massive update to the mechanics of the Possessed would be nice.<br /> <br /> <br /> You'll notice that I've talked a lot about &quot;updating mechanics.&quot; No where did I really mention talking about updating the <b><i>setting</i></b>. And that, really, is a huge drive behind updating most of the books we've gotten so far. Many of the settings have evolved over the years since the original core came out. Vampire using the lore past Requiem for Rome books takes a sharp deviation from the original line. Mage has evolved the Orders, the Seers, everyone. Promethean, even though a limited line, contains vastly different outlook in the later books than the core. Changeling, as well, has evolved to be based more on stories, its identity becoming firmer.<br /> <br /> What, then, has evolved in Inferno's sparse setting? You don't visit the Inferno, the Inferno visits us. The background is pretty much whatever fits the story you want it to, or more likely, the demons say that any story is true, lying about the whole thing, making it impossible to tell. What, beyond the mechanics, needs to be updated?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 02-06-2015, 10:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T08:54:49-08:00","id":394945,"title":"","content":"It's times like this I wish WoD would converge with the setting of d20's Infernum. Hell, we could do that! We could call it--<br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Shadows of Abaddon</b></span></div> <br /> <i>Demons are things that many people come to believe exist, in one shape or another. Ancient horrors from a realm of pure chaos and torment, wicked spirits that crave forbidden acts of violence and depravity, people with black hearts and no sense of moral compass\u2014these things and more are what people think of when they hear the word demon. But some wonder: if a creature like that of a demon can be evil, is it possible then that such a being can be drawn onto the path of enlightenment? How can there be evil demons if there are not good ones to define the former?<br /> <br /> Shadows of Abaddon is a setting that takes place with this in mind.<br /> <br /> Abaddon \u2013 the Eternal Nightmare<br /> In the language of the Hebrews, Abaddon is a term that roughly translates to \u201cdestruction\u201d or \u201cplace of destruction\u201d. The New Testament, however, depicts Abaddon as a fallen angel and ruler to an army of locusts. Within these two references are the symbols necessary to understand just what exactly Abaddon is to both humans and demons alike.<br /> <br /> Simply put: Abaddon is Hell.<br /> <br /> Ruled by eldritch beings known as the Archfiends, Abaddon is a place of perpetual torment and suffering, where the souls of the damned are funneled in from the Mortal Realm (also known as Mundus) and the Underworld to facilitate the stability of the plane.<br /> <br /> Since time immemorial, Abaddon has existed as something akin to a hurricane. At its center, known as Pandemonium, Abaddon is calm, but at the same time is it a prison to the most powerful of demons, known collectively as the Archfiends. Beyond the Inferno\u2014the barrier between the center and the rest of Abaddon\u2014chaos exists in the form of ever-shifting terrain and a warped sense of direction that\u2019s impossible to navigate through naturally.<br /> <br /> To counteract the instability of the plane, the demons uncovered the secrets of the Iliaster, the essence of the soul. With it, the fiends could temporarily stabilize \u201cregions\u201d of Abaddon in the form of colonies or even small city-states. But Iliaster was difficult to extract, it required ritualistic practices that proved too slow to counteract the nature of Abaddon. But demons are crafty. They soon decided that, instead of waiting for the souls to reach Hell, they would prepare them while they were still bound to Mundus.<br /> <br /> <b>The Nature of the Soul</b><br /> Souls are vital to the existence of demonic society. The Iliaster contained within them grants both stability to the Inferno, and the sense of intoxicating power over creation. Once all the Iliaster is siphoned, however, the soul disappears. Not even the demons know for sure where they go, some say they cease to exist, but others still feel that they are drawn away from Abaddon to an entirely different plane of existence altogether.<br /> <br /> As for Iliaster itself, it is just as enigmatic. Demons cannot produce it, for reasons not fully understood, but humans and other sentient creatures can. Theoretically, Iliaster is produced by the will of the soul, and thus, the soul of a strong-willed individual is highly craved by the Infernal. How then is a soul taken to Hell? Well, as it turns out, souls are drawn to other planes of existence that resonate with a similar &quot;character&quot; or &quot;mind set&quot; as the soul. Unfortunately, Abaddon is a highly negative and destructive plane, meaning demons have to augment the personality of mortals so that they are more in-tune with the Pit once the soul is permanently released from its physical form. That means turning people into assholes and sociopaths.<br /> <br /> Even when a demon succeeds in damning a soul to Hell, Abaddon's nature is to shift and turn, causing a high demand for souls that can't be met if the demons simply wait for things to happen. This leads to several courses of action being taken. One strategy is to create a cult. Cults procure cultists who siphon a bit of their soul on a regular basis to both their master, and Abaddon, without having to necessarily die. Best of all, the soul can repair itself! Meaning the iliaster doesn't run completely dry so long as the cultist is given time to recuperate! Granted, the amount of Iliaster this technique accumulates isn't very satisfying compared to getting it all at once, but still, it ensures at least something makes it to Abaddon.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T09:03:51-08:00","id":394968,"title":"","content":"Actually, there was an update to Inferno Demoms under a &quot;New Ephemeral Entity&quot; thread. I wrote a Condition for the process of a normal ephemeral becoming a Diabolus. <br /> <br /> The interesting thing was that Fiends can have traditional Virtues like Mercy as their Malapraxis, and feed an anyone giving into Vice as well as acting out their own. <br /> <br /> Hence, a good starting theme is the idea of passion gone mad and self-destructive. Noble or not, without focus and self awareness all aspirations turn dark.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T10:04:36-08:00","id":395074,"title":"","content":"I used Inferno for everything. My best recurring villain was one of the Possessed and demons make a great addition to any game (for me). Inferno had great resources for demons and dark things in all shapes and sizes. I would be extremely excited to see a new edition of Inferno.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/785-full-time-gm","name":"Full Time GM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T10:22:33-08:00","id":395092,"title":"","content":"I have to agree, I'm pretty sure Inferno is the only book we've used outside of the base rule book for every story we've had since we got it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T07:04:54-08:00","id":396301,"title":"","content":"[quote]<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/393536-inferno-2nd-edition?p=393971#post393971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As it is, each demon has a malpraxis, a vice and a thing. Moving away their vices from the Seven Sins simply allows for more demons, urging you to give into that vice to extreme degrees, or in situations where you shouldn't, or corrupting it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternatively, keep the big seven for the demons, representing the shape of their power - the way Inferno uses Vices for a power stat as well as power groupings - while retaining Integrity and its own internal sins to represent the resistance (and susceptibility) to the demon's malapraxis encroaching on the Possessed's psyche and personality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T17:54:48-08:00","id":398259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/393536-inferno-2nd-edition?p=394968#post394968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, there was an update to Inferno Demoms under a &quot;New Ephemeral Entity&quot; thread. I wrote a Condition for the process of a normal ephemeral becoming a Diabolus.<br /> <br /> The interesting thing was that Fiends can have traditional Virtues like Mercy as their Malapraxis, and feed an anyone giving into Vice as well as acting out their own.<br /> <br /> Hence, a good starting theme is the idea of passion gone mad and self-destructive. Noble or not, without focus and self awareness all aspirations turn dark.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/318864-more-ephemeral-entity-types\">You mean this thread, right here?</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T19:29:51-08:00","id":398306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/393536-inferno-2nd-edition?p=398259#post398259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/318864-more-ephemeral-entity-types\">You mean this thread, right here?</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That one. Couldn't link, I was on a phone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T14:21:53-08:00","id":399324,"title":"","content":"Actually the Wyrd does send avatars of sorts to kick your ass, it sends Nemisis to kill you if you mess with the Wyrd too much.<br /> <br /> I'll add the God Machine is kind of a force as well, abit one artifically created.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T14:38:41-08:00","id":399367,"title":"","content":"Personally I see Lust as more of a Virtue then a Vice. <br /> <br /> I think Inferno/Empyrean should become its own game line, called the Possessed: the Violation or something.<br /> <br /> Your Character is possessed by a Dominion with its own adgenda, with each Dominion type being a Splat. Infernals, Empyreans, Pychopomps, Divinities for example, and the other axis being portifilio, so you could have Vice, Virtue, Faith, Death for example, so you could have an Infernal with a portifolio of Death or an Empyrean with the Vice (say maybe the Empyrean uses lust say to tempt mortals away from true evil or something).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T14:48:02-08:00","id":399383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/393536-inferno-2nd-edition?p=399367#post399367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I see Lust as more of a Virtue then a Vice.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://img2.wikia.nocookie.net/__cb20140726023420/clashofclans/images/5/50/If-you-know-what-i-mean.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T08:28:16-08:00","id":403347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/393536-inferno-2nd-edition?p=393739#post393739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> First of all, lets try to be polite here.<br /> Secondly, yes, the Principle, the Wyrd, Fate and the Supernal are power forceses of nature, but therein lies the rub. They are forces of nature, like gravity. Its not like Fate or the Supernal will send an avatar of itself, to kick your ass because you fucked with its timeshare. The Principle might do that, but its just as likely to send an avatar of itself to bless you with divine strenght and good fortune because you fucked with said timeshare. Though it does have agents, they are as much a conundrum as the Principle itself, which remains incredibly vaguely defined.<br /> I dont know what &quot;The Devourer&quot; is, so I cant comment on that.<br /> <br /> None of the ones I commented on are as clearly defined and &quot;in your face&quot; as the God-Machine. The merest existance of them are a question not without its merit, whereas the God-Machine is visibly and tangibly real and out to get you.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> the point here is that the whole crossovers system isn't well thought off. The worlds and cosmologies don't fit well at the universal levels. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T08:38:03-08:00","id":403350,"title":"","content":"what I want to see is more crossover rules and staff for Mage x Inferno. I mean sorcerers and demons are nearly always mentioned together. least they could do is give a couple of pages for crossovers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T11:59:31-08:00","id":403566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/393536-inferno-2nd-edition?p=403350#post403350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what I want to see is more crossover rules and staff for Mage x Inferno. I mean sorcerers and demons are nearly always mentioned together.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only in Europe and places Europe spread its cultural zeitgeist; in most other cultures there isn't really a &quot;demon&quot; context, just things to which we apply the term &quot;demon&quot;(much like the word &quot;dragon,&quot; which we started applying to things like lung, ryu, but for some reason not the American unktehi and its ilk, despite their nearly identical appearance and cosmological significance, as well as association with rivers and poison). The idea of demonic entities based on the 'Seven Deadly Sins&quot; feels restrictive in a broader, global context, given that the mythological precision required by Inferno was so memetically tiny that it did not cover the vast capacity of the human imagination to invent terrors of its own folly and instead narrowed itself down to such a tiny fragment of even Christian ideology that the supplement was nearly useless on its own, unless you used it to describe, perhaps, a specific realm in Shadow or any of the broad Otherworlds already present, in which case you're better off seeing one of the supplements for that Otherworld in general. Talking about how the World of Darkness world doesn't fit well at the universal levels? That's great - Inferno doesn't fit at all, even at its <i>own </i>level.<br /> <br /> I mean - who's to say &quot;demons&quot; aren't conflated with fae, spirits, or ghosts, or all at the same time? Faerie legends were certainly integrated into Christian mythology as demons, that's where the whole thing about iron came from - Fae can't enter graveyards/holy places, most of those places used iron gates, so iron became the foe of the devil (so is salt - you're supposed to throw that shit over your left shoulder into the devil's face) - which, the idea of a fallen Lucifer is conflated from the story of an unnamed human Babylonian king associated with the astrological sign of Venus who was being poetically dissed by Isaiah. Baptists believe that any contact with ghosts is actually with demons in the shape of ghosts, and that the gods of Hinduism are creations by the devil to lead people who have never heard of their god astray, never mind that Hinduism is the oldest extant, still practiced religion in the world. Vampires can also very easily be conflated with demons - beings that are here by some cosmological fluke and represent the maddened desires of mortal flesh? Buddhism is rife with them, but they eat your shit, not your blood, which they take out of you through your stomach using their hands - but they are certainly capable of enslaving and corrupting mortals with their forbidden temptations.<br /> <br /> I guess my question is &quot;why?&quot; What would Inferno 2 do that, say, Dread Powers or Numina (or - dare I speak it? - a Tempter run out of Descent) don't do already?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T16:11:24-08:00","id":403813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>raygungoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/393536-inferno-2nd-edition?p=403566#post403566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Only in Europe and places Europe spread its cultural zeitgeist; in most other cultures there isn't really a &quot;demon&quot; context, just things to which we apply the term &quot;demon&quot;(much like the word &quot;dragon,&quot; which we started applying to things like lung, ryu, but for some reason not the American unktehi and its ilk, despite their nearly identical appearance and cosmological significance, as well as association with rivers and poison). The idea of demonic entities based on the 'Seven Deadly Sins&quot; feels restrictive in a broader, global context, given that the mythological precision required by Inferno was so memetically tiny that it did not cover the vast capacity of the human imagination to invent terrors of its own folly and instead narrowed itself down to such a tiny fragment of even Christian ideology that the supplement was nearly useless on its own, unless you used it to describe, perhaps, a specific realm in Shadow or any of the broad Otherworlds already present, in which case you're better off seeing one of the supplements for that Otherworld in general. Talking about how the World of Darkness world doesn't fit well at the universal levels? That's great - Inferno doesn't fit at all, even at its <i>own </i>level.<br /> <br /> <b>Right, stop right there. The idea of demons actually feeding on and embodying the Sins isn't a Judeo-Christian mythos idea either. That's a natural extension of nWoD spirits being able to feed on their respective domains; demons are spirits of Vice, so they feed on Vice. To everyone else, they look like they're causing chaos and doing evil for fun, which is kind of universal across human cultures. And the whole idea of them not fitting? Oh, that's a major problem with the book, yeah, real harsh criticism to <u>reiterate a core premise of the book, that even demons aren't entirely sure where they come from.</u> </b><br /> <br /> I mean - who's to say &quot;demons&quot; aren't conflated with fae, spirits, or ghosts, or all at the same time? Faerie legends were certainly integrated into Christian mythology as demons, that's where the whole thing about iron came from - Fae can't enter graveyards/holy places, most of those places used iron gates, so iron became the foe of the devil (so is salt - you're supposed to throw that shit over your left shoulder into the devil's face) - which, the idea of a fallen Lucifer is conflated from the story of an unnamed human Babylonian king associated with the astrological sign of Venus who was being poetically dissed by Isaiah. Baptists believe that any contact with ghosts is actually with demons in the shape of ghosts, and that the gods of Hinduism are creations by the devil to lead people who have never heard of their god astray, never mind that Hinduism is the oldest extant, still practiced religion in the world. Vampires can also very easily be conflated with demons - beings that are here by some cosmological fluke and represent the maddened desires of mortal flesh? Buddhism is rife with them, but they eat your shit, not your blood, which they take out of you through your stomach using their hands - but they are certainly capable of enslaving and corrupting mortals with their forbidden temptations.<br /> <br /> <b>I have to ask you, do you own the book? Demons can be all that, and more, it depends on the demon. Pretas themselves are an example demon, a race of Immundi who desperately want to become something else so they don't have to eat shit any more. The Furies are example demons, but they weren't always; no they were originally gods, just as it was with Astaroth; they went to the Inferno because there was nowhere else for them, and someone called them out so they could return to their duties. The Infernal is a category, not a race of fallen angels and their servants-Lucifer rubs elbows with Izanami, the Four Horsemen ride with rakashas on weekends, and Echidna regularly butts heads with Rangda over child care. Hell is all Hells, and wherever spirits and ghosts turn to malice, the Pit is there to welcome them. </b><br /> <br /> I guess my question is &quot;why?&quot; What would Inferno 2 do that, say, Dread Powers or Numina (or - dare I speak it? - a Tempter run out of Descent) don't do already?</div> </div> </div> </div>To create a ready race of antagonists, explore the idea of sin, rebellion, and evil, to decouple them from the idea of the Seven Deadly Sins, to really explore the ideology of people who spurn traditional religions so hard they worship their antithesis...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T17:39:25-08:00","id":403925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/393536-inferno-2nd-edition?p=403813#post403813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>The idea of demons actually feeding on and embodying the Sins isn't a Judeo-Christian mythos idea either.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Yes. They are.<br /> <br /> See how easy that is to <b><i>say</i></b>? I can get more specific: The very <i>idea </i>of sin is specifically Abrahamaic - you can accrue negative karma or even &quot;uncleanliness&quot; in, say, Hinduism or Shintoism, and you can do bad things, like, say attending black sings, in Navajo, and any number of other religions, but you only get &quot;sin,&quot; in regards to a violation of God's will that results in God casting one away into an empty darkness, in Abrahamaic religions (and you only get fire and brimstone after Dante writes some crazy revenge Bible fanfiction). It's very tidy for a book to just talk about how demons don't know where they come from, then sling around Christian esoteric terminology while completely avoiding almost every other cultural mythos from which they could have cribbed ideas. This is honestly why I didn't like the original vice system, either - the vices presented were presented as examples, but they got grabbed and run with so hard the entire system had to be reworked.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To create a ready race of antagonists, explore the idea of sin, rebellion, and evil, to decouple them from the idea of the Seven Deadly Sins, to really explore the ideology of people who spurn traditional religions so hard they worship their antithesis... </div> </div> </div>So, say, Tempters (who are that thing), Numina, Spirits, and Dread Powers honestly can't do that thing? Vampire can't do that thing? Geist could do that thing - it'd make a boss krewe.<br /> <br /> ...Getting away from this.<br /> <br /> Fleshing out the Shadow (and another Astral Realms book) in 2e could stand to happen. Abrahamaic faiths <i>are </i>pretty big in the modern world, and they're bound to have an impact on both, considering the way memes - especially ideas about the supernatural - fly around and mutate so rapidly in the modern world. What about splitting them up into MO or even feeding method, rather than a specific &quot;vice,&quot; like, this kind possesses people, this kind screws with minds, this kind stomps around like a big angry monster, this kind works through objects?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T19:39:01-08:00","id":404015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>raygungoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/393536-inferno-2nd-edition?p=403925#post403925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[/B]<br /> <br /> Yes. They are.<br /> <br /> See how easy that is to <b><i>say</i></b>? I can get more specific: The very <i>idea </i>of sin is specifically Abrahamaic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, stop, stop, stop.<br /> <br /> The <i>word</i> sin is Abrahamic, because its basis as <i>amrita </i>is a Jewish concept. The <i>concept, </i>however, ties into the very nature of religion. Yes, they may not call it sin, but <i>transgression against the moral code?</i> And there being <i>entities related to transgression against the moral code?</i><br /> <br /> That's a far older idea. Off the top of my head, I can think of negative karma and reincarnations of those who had a significant portion of it, the hungry ghosts stuck with devouring the thing that drove their previous self. Shinto has<i>amatsu tsumi, </i>crimes against all, and the figure of Ame-no-Kasageo, the wicked god of the pole star (who became identified with the star quite independently of Christianity). Even the Devil isn't something unique: the aforementioned Ame-no-Kasageo and Whiro, Maori God of Darkness, come to mind. The Faustian Bargain is all European, but Forbidden Knowledge is a Greek thing. <i>Inferno </i>posits they may all share a common power source...which is something a lot stranger than any story.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">So, say, Tempters (who are that thing)</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> No they aren't. Tempter/Saboteurs, maybe, but pure Tempters are defined by their neutrality on the whole God-Machine bit. They want to enjoy their free will and live a little for themselves, but they don't really want to revel in chaos and destructive freedom; they're hedonists, and they're called <i>Builders </i>for a reason. Tempters rest snugly at the center of their social webs, they don't embody the destructive passion the Inferno does. Besides the fact I was really talking about Infernal cultists, not demons themselves.<br /> <br /> For the others; Spirits are too inhuman, they don't have the strange sort of sympathy for humans the Inferno does. Vampires, a little more on the nose (hi there, Belial's Brood), but Sin-Eaters? A krewe developing that mythos honestly sounds like a more interesting story than actually dealing with them. <br /> <br /> So yeah, I do think Inferno has a niche as voices of Vice, but moving on...</span></span></span><br /> <br /> I do think we actually need to decouple the idea of Vice and &quot;evil&quot;. That <i>is </i>too Judeo-Christian, and while it is compelling, demons do need to seem like you might come out ahead out of game to really embrace the whole Infernal Bargaining system. Yes, the irony is that a fundamentally European concept needs to be decoupled from a European thing, but the story of Faust needs to be something a player thinks might be a smart idea-which is precisely the point, it seems smarter than it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T20:38:40-08:00","id":404065,"title":"","content":"Bear in mind that if we get a 2e-esque Inferno, it\u2019s going to be using 2e-esque Vices, which aren\u2019t so much about \u201cdoing evil things\u201d as \u201ctaking the easy way out\u201d: <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">A character's Vice, on the other hand, is a source of short-term comfort and a distraction from the world. Vice should be the easy way out, the sand he buries his head in, like a bully lashing out to avoid his own fear or an alcoholic drinking to forget.</span> Put another way, your Vice is the mechanism you use to cope with the problems in your life without actually dealing with them. <br /> <br /> Also, I don\u2019t really get the whole attitude of \u201coh, no! It\u2019s based on <i>Abrahamic concepts!</i> Unclean, unclean!\u201d Even if we were to posit that <b>Inferno</b> is fundamentally based on Abrahamic concepts (which I\u2019m only doing here for the sake of argument), what the heck is wrong with <i>that</i>? I mean, it\u2019s one thing to avoid enshrining a particular mythology or religion as being fundamentally true; but this attitude seems to reject not just that, but any connectns whatsoever to anything having to do with said religion(s) \u2014 it seems to be overcompensating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-12-2015, 11:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T04:53:50-08:00","id":404384,"title":"","content":"As far as WoD goes the general premise seems to be that every religion gets something right, but no religion gets everything right. Demons are Christianity's &quot;something right&quot;. The Shadow and Hedge and the dozen or so God-things are it's &quot;not everything right&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T05:10:55-08:00","id":404389,"title":"","content":"I think the concept of vice (lust, greed) is tied to human nature, and thus can be applied to any cultural or religious background.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T06:04:35-08:00","id":405740,"title":"","content":"The inherent problem with the Inferno is its <i>universal</i> nature wherein it positions itself as the <i>source</i> of all these entities. Oni, for example, are mentioned as languishing on piles of bones in the Inferno when, quite frankly, the attitudes of the Oni (and indeed many if not all Eastern wicked spirits) are more in line with the attitudes of the <i>True Fae.</i> That is to say, the mentality of these entities is supposed to be alien and destructive in that the entity in itself encourages destructive attitudes out of an inability to do anything else.<br /> <br /> The (new) World of Darkness is full of alien forces encountering the familiar and twisting them in strange and bizarre ways. The God-Machine does this, the True Fae do this, the Spirits do this. <i>Inferno</i> attempts to bring a familiar element - <i>human evil - </i>into the scenario and then make that evil supernatural (something already achieved by malevolent ghosts) <i>but also inhuman and alien. </i><br /> <br /> Mechanically, the creatures that reside in Inferno are just mean ghosts. They are a creature of murder that encourages people to murder so that it can drag them into its own torment. Just like the ghost of a slasher might linger after his passing and encourage the birth of a copy-cat killer. Functionally then we see, both within the narrative and the mechanics of the game, there is little that differentiates the Infernal from a malignant ghost or spirit.<br /> <br /> Indeed the book even suggests the already present element of the malignant spirit - the Maeljin from Werewolf - are likely these selfsame entities. If Immundi are like Maeljin of another name, both functionally and fictionally, and the Larvals are just malignant ghosts in the same respect we're only left with the supposed distinctive qualities of the Dominion. However, what separates a Dominion from an Immundi? Both are ephemeral entities, both have rank, both rely heavily on Vice. Within the context of their own rules both even use the &quot;Malapraxis&quot; and &quot;Demonic Universal Traits&quot;.<br /> <br /> Within the context of the updated second-edition ephemeral creatures rules this becomes even more obfuscated. Spirits can already embody any and all vices. A spirit is fueled entirely, as its sole motivating existence, by its nature. Anything relating to this nature, in any distinct way is <i>Resonant</i> with the spirit. Therefore if its nature is vice then is it not just one of these above mentioned &quot;demons&quot;? What makes a Dominion <i>different</i> from a malevolent spirit <i>other</i> that the fact that it comes from a place called &quot;Inferno&quot; and possessed a certain set of rules in the previous edition? If a spirit is a &quot;Spirit of Lust&quot; then anywhere - from nightclubs to brothels - will resonate with it. People behaving in reckless pursuit of their desires, especially bodily, will resonate with it. It will regain essence and willpower as easily as any demon of the Inferno, its more or less mechanically functioning like one, isn't it?<br /> <br /> While contrary to my above argument I took the time to convert Dominions (and to a lesser extent Larvals and Immundi) into the new rules - that conversion was mostly just creating a dependent condition (similar to Resonant), setting up the demonic traits - which really are just numina - as things that all demons possessed (like the Liars Tongue) and lastly a manifestation power to cause and improve their dependent condition. In doing this I noticed very little actual difference between them and a Spirit mechanically. Really it all came down to the <i>trappings</i> and that isn't really worth a new book, is it?<br /> <br /> In the end I noticed there was only one thing I truly liked and felt supported Infernals as something different: <i>the whisperer</i>. This I felt translated best as a condition. I also felt it lent better to the idea presented in the whisperer section's sidebar; the demons aren't &quot;real&quot;. They're born of human thought. As the Buddhists imagine, we make our own demons, and therein lies why they might be deserving of some separation from spirits. Spirits aren't born of our interaction with the world around us. They spontaneously come into being through presence and absorbing energies. But a whisperer pops up when your psyche shatters, something slips up through the cracks of your growing insanity and whispers into your ear for you to break the status quo.<br /> <br /> I have recently found myself finding the Inferno and its inhabitants rather redundant. Between Spirits, the God-Machine's ever deceptive angels and their fallen counterparts, and malevolent ghosts any group of mortals, hunters or even magi have everything they could want and more to bind up with the Lesser Key of Solomon and flick holy water at and hell, it might work on some of them too, who knows? The only thing I really find myself clinging to and still thoroughly enjoying from the book is the idea that a Whisperer might latch onto somebody when they take an integrity hit and become something new. No ancient evil from the birth of creation, but something young and fresh, a day old evil that crawls about gorging itself desperately in a dim hope of survival before fading away or infecting something else.<br /> <br /> Bringing my post back to the beginning. Why does the book present the Inferno as <i>human evil</i> when it is another dimension full of alien monsters that don't really understand our world and just want to destroy it? Why are they so much like us? They sound like the True Fae to me, just ones that like to throw up the horns and wreak a little havoc before they drag you to their weird, conceptual world of nightmare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T06:49:34-08:00","id":405753,"title":"","content":"I don't think that Inferno's universal nature is a problem. My feeling from the book was always that demons are not meant to be a &quot;thing of their own&quot;, but a symbol for corruption. They are &quot;just&quot; evil spirits, mad ghosts and dreams who got out of control. The Whisperer is the way Hell continues to corrupt others, feeding upon them to expand itself. Inferno can't create anything, but must feeds on the rest of the World of Darkness in order to exist.<br /> <br /> The point is that not every dark spirit of evil ghost is a demon. Many are just what they are. A demon is what happens when Inferno touch them, lures them and devours them. Hell is a parasitic entity which needs to feed upon morality to survive. A &quot;spirit of Lust&quot; could be a regular entity of the Shadow until one day it hears a whisper- and that whisper grants it a bit more freedom. It still acts according to its nature, but for a change, it really enjoys it. It becomes aware, gaining freedom- and freedom allows it to fall. That is, from my point of view, the point of Hell in WoD. It is a realm of free will- and its consequences. As long as a spirit, a ghost or a geotia does something &quot;evil&quot; without knowing it is evil, they are immune to its effect, but when they do the same thing while knowing- that's when Inferno may corrupt them.<br /> <br /> This is the point of Hell- it doesn't want to destroy us. It loves us. Really, it loves us so much it can each us up! It is filled with passion and hate and rage and care. It can just eat us up! It loves the fact that we are free, and that we can act against the rules we ourselves enforced. While it spread evil, it isn't about just evil- but about transgression. It is a separate, made realm sure- but a very human one. Inferno understands mankind, or else its Whisperers would have done pretty bad job. It is a realm made out of our own evil, out of our own choices. At first it may have been nothing more then a collection of Whisperers- but after feeding upon human morality for ages it became a &quot;real&quot; place- as far as a Lower Depth can be called &quot;real&quot;. Its denizens know what they are doing- we are not toys or pets seen from some twisted point of view of beautiful madness. We are like cattle for them- they know what they are doing. This is the realm of human evil, not alien evil.<br /> <br /> At least, that's how I see it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T07:32:33-08:00","id":405776,"title":"","content":"For me, the best representation of how Inferno\u00b4s demons should be is despicted in the videogame <i>&quot;The Suffering&quot;</i> and its sequel <i>&quot;The Suffering: Ties That Bind&quot;</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9Wa17JMqN7Q\" data-code=\"9Wa17JMqN7Q\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/9Wa17JMqN7Q/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> In the settings, the demons, called Malefactors by the experts, are the souls of sinners twisted after their deaths and/or the manifestation of their sins. They prey on human suffering and murder, specially the one which aligns with their particular sin.<br /> The protagonist is a tormented fugitive with a personal Mr.Hyde-like Malefactor attached, who must find a balance between survival and sanity while trying to accomplish his goal (either revenge or redemption).<br /> Leaving aside the shooter theme, the most interesting part is the villain: <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">is actually a split personality from the protagonist, who began as an imaginary friend &quot;teaching&quot; him and turning his life toward crime until he became powerful enough to take control at occasions, and eventually escaped outside</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 02-14-2015, 10:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T08:07:41-08:00","id":405808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/393536-inferno-2nd-edition?p=405753#post405753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the point of Hell- it doesn't want to destroy us. It loves us. Really, it loves us so much it can each us up! It is filled with passion and hate and rage and care. It can just eat us up! It loves the fact that we are free, and that we can act against the rules we ourselves enforced. While it spread evil, it isn't about just evil- but about transgression. It is a separate, made realm sure- but a very human one. Inferno understands mankind, or else its Whisperers would have done pretty bad job. It is a realm made out of our own evil, out of our own choices. At first it may have been nothing more then a collection of Whisperers- but after feeding upon human morality for ages it became a &quot;real&quot; place- as far as a Lower Depth can be called &quot;real&quot;. Its denizens know what they are doing- we are not toys or pets seen from some twisted point of view of beautiful madness. We are like cattle for them- they know what they are doing. This is the realm of human evil, not alien evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. When all other Ephemera Entites of WoD are more alien, Hell is build on humans thought and restriction.<br /> <br /> <b>Shadow spirits</b> - they are just spiritual animals, competing for Essence ( the food ) and wanting to come higher and higher in pecking order.<br /> <br /> <b>Twillight ghosts</b> - they are only echoes of our lives, memories on auto play. They are not truly creative.<br /> <br /> <b>Goetia beings</b> - they are dreams made shape, they do not have human thought in them.<br /> <br /> <b>True Fae</b> - they are mad gods of rules made eons before. They do not create or understand humanity.<br /> <br /> <b>God Machine</b> - is alien entity wanting World of Darkness as it is. It's called, calculating. But it does not have human passion.<br /> <br /> In this light, Hell is something other:<br /> <br /> <b>Inferno's demons</b> - they are all about Ephemera beings corrupted by human transgression. The are Shadow spirits fixated on humans sins - and <b>only</b> humans as food and power source. They are ghosts twisted by Vice so much, they regain intelligence, they remind more active, living being than it's memory. Corrupted Goetia reason with primal archetypes of humanity, becoming like humans in the process. In theory, Fae also could Fall, but by this, they would be not Fea - they would need to become <i>more</i> human-like, and they all power an being is based on how <i>alien</i> they are. Maybe changelings are demons of the Fae? God Machine's Unchained are, at least in part, the Inferno's staple on it - when Machine get's Emotions, it becomes like humans, and stop being Machine.<br /> <br /> All of this is because humans love to sin ( i.e. break their own rules of society )...<br /> <br /> And, what's weird, all of this can be said about Heaven ( the Empyrean ) and it's relation to various Ephemera.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-14-2015, 11:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T15:12:46-08:00","id":406136,"title":"","content":"Wow. This thread exploded lately, hasn't it? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DesolateDolly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/393536-inferno-2nd-edition?p=405740#post405740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the end I noticed there was only one thing I truly liked and felt supported Infernals as something different: <i>the whisperer</i>. This I felt translated best as a condition. I also felt it lent better to the idea presented in the whisperer section's sidebar; the demons aren't &quot;real&quot;. They're born of human thought. As the Buddhists imagine, we make our own demons, and therein lies why they might be deserving of some separation from spirits. Spirits aren't born of our interaction with the world around us. They spontaneously come into being through presence and absorbing energies. But a whisperer pops up when your psyche shatters, something slips up through the cracks of your growing insanity and whispers into your ear for you to break the status quo.</div> </div> </div> </div> Personally, I always thought whisperers were always redundant with the Goetic magic, ala mage. This kind of &quot;whisperer&quot; action is the kind of thing I envision the astral summons working out. The astral beings (now called Goetics in 2e) work on nibbling at the holes in your soul to gain their Essence, won't they? Feeding off your fears, insecurities, and personal madness? <br /> <br /> While I like the idea of a little shard of a demon that can't do more than just whisper temptations, I kinda think its still redundant. That's just me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/393536-inferno-2nd-edition?p=405808#post405808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree. When all other Ephemera Entites of WoD are more alien, Hell is build on humans thought and restriction.</div> </div> </div> </div> And this is actually why I think of Infernal demons as Hunter spirits. Hunter, for all their slaying of other supernaturals, is at its core about humans committing transgressions and becoming monsters themselves. Your cumulative sins not only slowly turning into a monster, but giving birth to more monsters. <br /> <br /> At its heart, the Inferno is kind of like the line, &quot;you can't fight the devil with his own tools without becoming his sword.&quot; Its about the inevitable corruption that comes in a world where you have to make transgressions to survive. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Shadow spirits</b> - they are just spiritual animals, competing for Essence ( the food ) and wanting to come higher and higher in pecking order.<br /> <br /> <b>Twillight ghosts</b> - they are only echoes of our lives, memories on auto play. They are not truly creative.<br /> <br /> <b>Goetia beings</b> - they are dreams made shape, they do not have human thought in them.<br /> <br /> <b>True Fae</b> - they are mad gods of rules made eons before. They do not create or understand humanity.<br /> <br /> <b>God Machine</b> - is alien entity wanting World of Darkness as it is. It's called, calculating. But it does not have human passion. </div> </div> </div> With all due respect, this kind of oversimplifies things and misses the point of many of these. Spirits may compete for food, but they are highly intelligent. As well, they are animistic reflections - meaning, they are the spiritual embodiment of concepts, including human concepts of like the very Spirit of America. Ghosts are hardly &quot;just echoes.&quot; Any ghost above rank 1 is a sentient being in its own right, very likely a significant chunk of the human soul unable to pass on (yes, its missing that supernal piece mages focus on, but that's not the whole of the soul). As per mage writers, Goetic beings aren't dreams - that's more of a fae thing. They're literally soul shards. They are literally made of human thought and experiences in part. The Gentry are creatures inexorably tied to human dreams and fantasies and stories - there's a very good chance they didn't exist until humanity did, and are born from humanity.<br /> <br /> God Machine is pretty spot on, though. And that's kind of the point, though. Demon: the Descent is the only game out there that involves truly inhuman characters. Vampires and Mummies were once human with still human memories. Werewolves tell themselves they were never human, but that's just a semantics argument over the definition of &quot;humanity.&quot; Mages, well. Changelings are part human, part fae. Geist: the Sin-Eaters have humans sharing a body with a death-god. Hunters are humans. Even Prometheans, despite being non-humans, are driven to becoming like them. <br /> <br /> Only DtD really involves character that, in no way, are human, have never been human, will never be human. It makes sense that their angelic cousins would be even more alien. Everything else, in some way, reflects some aspect of humanity or, barring that, a part of humanity's understanding of nature. Even the Abyssal beings that make their way into reality have to define themselves in terms of humanity's abuses (seriously, there's one that comes into being when you fudge accounting books and messes with numbers, while another literally gets off from spousal abuse). <br /> <br /> The WoD is very much a human centric universe; unsurprising, considering that the Storytelling system is about telling stories, which are always reflections of the tellers. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Inferno's demons</b> - they are all about Ephemera beings corrupted by human transgression. The are Shadow spirits fixated on humans sins - and <b>only</b> humans as food and power source. They are ghosts twisted by Vice so much, they regain intelligence, they remind more active, living being than it's memory. Corrupted Goetia reason with primal archetypes of humanity, becoming like humans in the process. In theory, Fae also could Fall, but by this, they would be not Fea - they would need to become <i>more</i> human-like, and they all power an being is based on how <i>alien</i> they are. Maybe changelings are demons of the Fae? God Machine's Unchained are, at least in part, the Inferno's staple on it - when Machine get's Emotions, it becomes like humans, and stop being Machine.<br /> <br /> All of this is because humans love to sin ( i.e. break their own rules of society )...<br /> <br /> And, what's weird, all of this can be said about Heaven ( the Empyrean ) and it's relation to various Ephemera. </div> </div> </div> Ahh... setting aside the issues I have with your descriptions of other ephemeral beings, but where are you getting all that about the Empyrean? <br /> <br /> Empyrean beings are defined as going back to being alien entities. &quot;You\u2019d rather your character be possessed by something truly alien, something truly and utterly incomprehensible. You\u2019d rather your character be possessed by an angel.&quot; The Empyrean is going back to being more like the qashmal or God Machine angel level of alien, or even perhaps Supernal seraphim/cherubim, if not one of those three options. Where infernal demons reflect human desires unbound, angels .... don't. Demons are selfish, angels are obsessed with a Plan.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T19:14:49-08:00","id":406247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/393536-inferno-2nd-edition?p=405753#post405753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that Inferno's universal nature is a problem. My feeling from the book was always that demons are not meant to be a &quot;thing of their own&quot;, but a symbol for corruption. They are &quot;just&quot; evil spirits, mad ghosts and dreams who got out of control. The Whisperer is the way Hell continues to corrupt others, feeding upon them to expand itself. Inferno can't create anything, but must feeds on the rest of the World of Darkness in order to exist.<br /> <br /> The point is that not every dark spirit of evil ghost is a demon. Many are just what they are. A demon is what happens when Inferno touch them, lures them and devours them. Hell is a parasitic entity which needs to feed upon morality to survive. A &quot;spirit of Lust&quot; could be a regular entity of the Shadow until one day it hears a whisper- and that whisper grants it a bit more freedom. It still acts according to its nature, but for a change, it really enjoys it. It becomes aware, gaining freedom- and freedom allows it to fall. That is, from my point of view, the point of Hell in WoD. It is a realm of free will- and its consequences. As long as a spirit, a ghost or a geotia does something &quot;evil&quot; without knowing it is evil, they are immune to its effect, but when they do the same thing while knowing- that's when Inferno may corrupt them.<br /> <br /> This is the point of Hell- it doesn't want to destroy us. It loves us. Really, it loves us so much it can each us up! It is filled with passion and hate and rage and care. It can just eat us up! It loves the fact that we are free, and that we can act against the rules we ourselves enforced. While it spread evil, it isn't about just evil- but about transgression. It is a separate, made realm sure- but a very human one. Inferno understands mankind, or else its Whisperers would have done pretty bad job. It is a realm made out of our own evil, out of our own choices. At first it may have been nothing more then a collection of Whisperers- but after feeding upon human morality for ages it became a &quot;real&quot; place- as far as a Lower Depth can be called &quot;real&quot;. Its denizens know what they are doing- we are not toys or pets seen from some twisted point of view of beautiful madness. We are like cattle for them- they know what they are doing. This is the realm of human evil, not alien evil.<br /> <br /> At least, that's how I see it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, everything you said there is <i>trappings</i> and not <i>mechanics</i> either narrative or rules.<br /> <br /> To bring clarity to my previous post: We're discussing here the topic of whether World of Darkness: Inferno should have merit in gaining a second edition update of some kind and what shape that update might take. My argument was that it doesn't need one because, at this point, it is functionally only useful for its <i>setting</i>.<br /> <br /> It creates a specific fiction regarding these entities that some might specifically enjoy - that of the ceaselessly hungry maw at the bottom of creation and the things living between its teeth.<br /> <br /> But the mechanics of its entities are functionally identical - both in their behaviour in the narrative and their behaviour in the game - as entities already present in the World of Darkness. In the end the Lust Spirit example suffers from the problem of: if it quacks like a duck, it looks like a duck, and it flutters about like a duck, maybe it isn't actually a beautiful swan?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T22:16:16-08:00","id":406368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/393536-inferno-2nd-edition?p=406136#post406136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And this is actually why I think of Infernal demons as Hunter spirits. Hunter, for all their slaying of other supernaturals, is at its core about humans committing transgressions and becoming monsters themselves. Your cumulative sins not only slowly turning into a monster, but giving birth to more monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree on here with you - always felt that Hunters demons are Infernal, in reality. Maybe we will have real update with Vigil 2ed?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/393536-inferno-2nd-edition?p=406136#post406136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At its heart, the Inferno is kind of like the line, &quot;you can't fight the devil with his own tools without becoming his sword.&quot; Its about the inevitable corruption that comes in a world where you have to make transgressions to survive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also agree on that. &quot;Sin&quot; is just nice name for &quot;transgression of rules&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/393536-inferno-2nd-edition?p=406136#post406136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With all due respect, this kind of oversimplifies things and misses the point of many of these. Spirits may compete for food, but they are highly intelligent. As well, they are animistic reflections - meaning, they are the spiritual embodiment of concepts, including human concepts of like the very Spirit of America. Ghosts are hardly &quot;just echoes.&quot; Any ghost above rank 1 is a sentient being in its own right, very likely a significant chunk of the human soul unable to pass on (yes, its missing that supernal piece mages focus on, but that's not the whole of the soul). As per mage writers, Goetic beings aren't dreams - that's more of a fae thing. They're literally soul shards. They are literally made of human thought and experiences in part. The Gentry are creatures inexorably tied to human dreams and fantasies and stories - there's a very good chance they didn't exist until humanity did, and are born from humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, in reality, it does not. Yes, you can have very &quot;inteligent&quot; or &quot;higher&quot; Shadow spirits. thinking in quasi-humans way - but their <i>raison d'\u00eatre</i>? To be on the top of foodchain - even Luna, Firstborns or probably Gaia - they all do what they do from the same reasons like lowerest mote - to promote their Essence connected to their Influnaces. On the level they are they have many ( and I mean <b>many</b> ) aspects of reality as their Essence generation, so the thing like Luna is Widow, Mother, Fickle Woman, Queen of Night, Destroyer, Dreamer, Seer, Trickster or Shadow ( yes, also as the Shadow of Shadow Realm ), It's all true - but from the Shadow Realm ecology stand point - she only is this things only to generate and claim more Essence for her, even if she does not conciess about it. You do not tell me Lunes are more thing than living automata of spiritual service - they can have personality, even elobarate. But in the end, all spirits are &quot;animals&quot; competing over recourse of Essence, even if we talk about abstract choirs.<br /> <br /> Same goes with Ghosts and Goetia - yes, they can work as &quot;fuller personality&quot;. But their basic role in nWoD cosmology, what <b>they are</b> - is only living ( but thinking ) memories and souls pices. They are not humans or &quot;spirits oh humanity&quot;. Strangely, the Inferno, in WoD reality, <b>is</b>. Inferno only mirrors the things why humanity is even on itself so screwd in WoD - that humans can be <i>evil</i> on they own, they can <b>transgress</b> they own rules. And when this idea &quot;pollut&quot; other Ephemera, making it's basic sustain - we get a demon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/393536-inferno-2nd-edition?p=406136#post406136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The WoD is very much a human centric universe; unsurprising, considering that the Storytelling system is about telling stories, which are always reflections of the tellers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not question this - I only pointing that Ephemera <i>are</i> alien, even if they are hiding it. They are entites messing with humanity general state. ONLY the <b>Inferno</b> loves humans as they are - because Hell's demons are, in reality, &quot;Ephemera made as humans&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/393536-inferno-2nd-edition?p=406136#post406136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Empyrean beings are defined as going back to being alien entities. &quot;You\u2019d rather your character be possessed by something truly alien, something truly and utterly incomprehensible. You\u2019d rather your character be possessed by an angel.&quot; The Empyrean is going back to being more like the qashmal or God Machine angel level of alien, or even perhaps Supernal seraphim/cherubim, if not one of those three options. Where infernal demons reflect human desires unbound, angels .... don't. Demons are selfish, angels are obsessed with a Plan.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on the beings you describe. Qashmal or God Machine - sure, their ae about Plan. But the Empyrean angels described in Inferno? They are about <i>Virtues</i> - they are abuot <i>rules</i> the humanity governec <i>itself</i>. If Hells demons are about overthrowing rules of society, the Empyrean angels are about fortifing them, overthrowing them on those that do not want them. Chaos and Order, only on human scale.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DesolateDolly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/393536-inferno-2nd-edition?p=406247#post406247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the mechanics of its entities are functionally identical - both in their behaviour in the narrative and their behaviour in the game - as entities already present in the World of Darkness. In the end the Lust Spirit example suffers from the problem of: if it quacks like a duck, it looks like a duck, and it flutters about like a duck, maybe it isn't actually a beautiful swan?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is desctinctive - Lust Spirit ( lower one ) is half conciuse on it's actions. It want, literally, to get ( others to ) fuck. He is animialisitc in this. He does not make very eleborate plans and, hell no, work with some &quot;rules&quot;, or even break them. He <i>does not see</i> &quot;the rules&quot;. Inferno demons are all about <i>breaking</i> the rules. They get humans have marriages. They get humanity have idea of love. Binding of souls and all that. And they <i>love</i> it. Beacuse when there are rules, there is <i>transgression</i>, &quot;sin&quot;. Lust Spirit overrides women and makes her in to animal frenzy when she will fuck with any man she can meet - it's not picky, it just need Essence. Lust Demon will go to her and husbands apartment, call the hubby to come earlier - only to invite him to the orgy she made in mean time. Demon her &quot;won&quot; twice - it shakes the foundation of marriage, the monogamy they oath in the wedding day. And if husband liked the orgy, but was reclusive on the start, demon also broke <i>his</i> rules.<br /> <br /> Like I said earlier - Shadow spirits are &quot;animals&quot; of spirit world. Demons are very much the &quot;humans&quot; of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T22:17:59-08:00","id":406369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DesolateDolly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/393536-inferno-2nd-edition?p=406247#post406247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unfortunately, everything you said there is <i>trappings</i> and not <i>mechanics</i> either narrative or rules.<br /> <br /> To bring clarity to my previous post: We're discussing here the topic of whether World of Darkness: Inferno should have merit in gaining a second edition update of some kind and what shape that update might take. My argument was that it doesn't need one because, at this point, it is functionally only useful for its <i>setting</i>.<br /> <br /> It creates a specific fiction regarding these entities that some might specifically enjoy - that of the ceaselessly hungry maw at the bottom of creation and the things living between its teeth.<br /> <br /> But the mechanics of its entities are functionally identical - both in their behaviour in the narrative and their behaviour in the game - as entities already present in the World of Darkness. In the end the Lust Spirit example suffers from the problem of: if it quacks like a duck, it looks like a duck, and it flutters about like a duck, maybe it isn't actually a beautiful swan?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the Lust demon is not a duck. He may have been a duck at some point, but now he's a seagull who's very good at pretending he's a duck.Beneath the surface the gull is a lot smarter than the duck, and understands the fact that the humans who give him bread have lives and minds of their own beyond his seagull-centric mind, and they will give him more stuff if he plays to human sensibilities of cuteness, hence why he's wearing a duck disguise. People despise seagulls, but ducks? Ducks get the good bread. He's saving up to turn himself into a parrot one day, really start getting attention and care from humans-maybe even a human friend.<br /> <br /> That's the Second Edition impetus right there; to emphasize the fact that the demonic mind is what differentiates a demon from everyone else, their greatest strength and weakness. Because it's a <i>human </i>mind, capable of self-reflection, growth, and the desire to be more than it is. That's what makes the Infernal truly dangerous, because the Inferno is humanity at its darkest-which also contains the potential for humanity at its brightest.<br /> <br /> Besides, alien evil is a dime a dozen. We have an entire race of that in a major gameline, the Strix. Give me the dark side of humanity made flesh, the embodiments of selfishness and self-destructive behaviors. At this point, the monsters that aren't actually that Lovecraftian are the new and novel thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T23:08:11-08:00","id":406385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/393536-inferno-2nd-edition?p=406369#post406369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because the Lust demon is not a duck. He may have been a duck at some point, but now he's a seagull who's very good at pretending he's a duck.Beneath the surface the gull is a lot smarter than the duck, and understands the fact that the humans who give him bread have lives and minds of their own beyond his seagull-centric mind, and they will give him more stuff if he plays to human sensibilities of cuteness, hence why he's wearing a duck disguise. People despise seagulls, but ducks? Ducks get the good bread. He's saving up to turn himself into a parrot one day, really start getting attention and care from humans-maybe even a human friend.<br /> <br /> That's the Second Edition impetus right there; to emphasize the fact that the demonic mind is what differentiates a demon from everyone else, their greatest strength and weakness. Because it's a <i>human </i>mind, capable of self-reflection, growth, and the desire to be more than it is. That's what makes the Infernal truly dangerous, because the Inferno is humanity at its darkest-which also contains the potential for humanity at its brightest.<br /> <br /> Besides, alien evil is a dime a dozen. We have an entire race of that in a major gameline, the Strix. Give me the dark side of humanity made flesh, the embodiments of selfishness and self-destructive behaviors. At this point, the monsters that aren't actually that Lovecraftian are the new and novel thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately all that you said is once again <i>setting</i> and not <i>narrative mechanic. </i>The hidden motivation of a demon - and it is hidden since they're <i>perfect liars</i> (which itself is an <i>inhuman</i> trait, but I digress) - ensures that player characters are seldom going to uncover this modus operandi which presents a problem: If the players cannot distinguish the Lust Spirit from the Lust Demon it doesn't matter that the Lust Demon has all these beautiful emotions and greedy little desires while the Lust Spirit is more straight forward (a fact that itself is not universally true - spirits are not <i>animal intelligences</i> unless they are <i>spirits comparable to an animal</i>). There is <i>zero </i>reason that a spirit whose central nature is a <i>human emotion</i> and that he resonates and feeds off of this emotion (in this case Lust) <i>is by necessity inhuman in its outlook in any way that the demon equivalent may be considered human its outlook.</i> Or, put another way, saying a spirit is inhuman when it feeds off of human emotion and behaves on and empowers that human emotion - thus behaving in an altogether familiar and human way - is inaccurate and simply calling something alien because if it's alien it's different.<br /> <br /> Remember: Writing up a complex and long set of motivations for an entity is fine if these details are revealed to the player characters in any meaningful way but unless these details <i>clearly</i> illustrate the behaviour of the entity to the character then they aren't really <i>different mechanics</i>. They're just bells and whistles. If the thing serves the same role in the story, kills the same people, in the same way, fights the player characters in the same fashion and dies in the same spectacular display then whether that thing comes from Inferno or Shadow is ultimately decoration.<br /> <br /> A Dominion needs to feed its vice to survive, to grow and to continue to become greater. It behaves thus like a spirit in that it hunts down areas resonant with itself, feeds on them, while destroying or damaging them and then if it encounters other denizens of twilight - like other spirits or ghosts - it infects these entities, devours them or inherently changes them into itself. This is absolutely the same Darwinnian behaviour found in Spirits. That a Dominion is capable of more complex consideration doesn't separate it from a spirit as a spirit is perfectly capable of being very clever.<br /> <br /> Now certainly, if you <i>like</i> the <i>details or setting</i> of Inferno as a Hell-Realm where evil spirit entities called Dominions and Immundi and Larvals emerge to wreck their havoc on the world then have at it. However, I would argue that they don't require a <i>new book</i> until something really separates them from what we currently have represented in our Ephemeral Creatures rules. At current, I can make a spirit and a dominion and my Hunter players would have a hard time telling them apart if I don't decorate them differently but the same can't be said for a ghost when compared to a spirit, angel or strix because they're mechanically behaving differently - both in the narrative and in the rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T01:14:02-08:00","id":406498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DesolateDolly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/393536-inferno-2nd-edition?p=406385#post406385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now certainly, if you <i>like</i> the <i>details or setting</i> of Inferno as a Hell-Realm where evil spirit entities called Dominions and Immundi and Larvals emerge to wreck their havoc on the world then have at it. However, I would argue that they don't require a <i>new book</i> until something really separates them from what we currently have represented in our Ephemeral Creatures rules. At current, I can make a spirit and a dominion and my Hunter players would have a hard time telling them apart if I don't decorate them differently but the same can't be said for a ghost when compared to a spirit, angel or strix because they're mechanically behaving differently - both in the narrative and in the rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe the rules of interaction? Spirits need the Resonance to build up. The Demons should interact when &quot;Sins&quot; (Transgressions ) of their Malepraxies come to being. If Spirit of Lust comes when people make a Night Club in reality the Dark Room to randomly fuck with each other - the Demon of List comes when perfect marriage is destroyed by the act of infidelity, killing the wife in perverted way. Spirits need build up, Hell's Demons need atrocities. I think it would change all &quot;we need this and those Conditions&quot; mechanics enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-15-2015, 09:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T06:23:23-08:00","id":406614,"title":"","content":"Inferno Demosn do have mechanical differences from either of the other spiritual entities they can corrupt, so no, I don't think their niche is already covered by others. Is not only a matter of setting, but even if it was it would have been enough to warrant a second edition update.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T08:58:48-08:00","id":406736,"title":"","content":"If we were to talk strictly mechanics and not fluff, here is what would need to be updated:<ul><li>the details of Ephemeral Conditions for Demons</li> <li>how Malapraxes work with Vices that are not easily tied to the Seven Deadlies</li> <li>(special modifications for Mystery Cult Initiation for Infernal cults)</li> <li>updated rules for their Dark Numina</li> <li>how exactly demons interact with Integrity* and reworked Integrity traits</li> <li>what demons can offer Sin-Eaters, Mummies and ... uh... Demons and Beasts</li> <li>updated rules for Possessed**</li> </ul><br /> *: Having a demon be able to use Utter Damnation to claim the soul of a poor sod who happened to drop to Integrity 1 because he witnessed Supernal Magic seems... unfair...<br /> **: Experience Costs, updated/new Vestments (some mechanics do not work well anymore in 2e)<br /> <br /> <br /> If they wanted to add more new stuff, there is actually quite a bit of room left (as others have mentioned before):<ul><li>more on L'enfant Diabolique!</li> <li>Empyrean! They could even make that the theme of the book; &quot;Heaven or Hell, LET'S ROCK&quot;</li> <li>many new Merits!</li> <li>new Conditions!</li> <li>new Dark Numina and Vestments!</li> <li>teases about how the Inferno might interact with stuff like the Underworld, Duat, the God-Machine and so on</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T10:09:15-08:00","id":406802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DesolateDolly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/393536-inferno-2nd-edition?p=406385#post406385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember: Writing up a complex and long set of motivations for an entity is fine if these details are revealed to the player characters in any meaningful way but unless these details <i>clearly</i> illustrate the behaviour of the entity to the character then they aren't really <i>different mechanics</i>. They're just bells and whistles. If the thing serves the same role in the story, kills the same people, in the same way, fights the player characters in the same fashion and dies in the same spectacular display then whether that thing comes from Inferno or Shadow is ultimately decoration.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite. That's why I advocate a different idea; focus on the demons and not the people who pact with them. Show what it's like to be Mephistopheles from his side of the pentagram, how a demon thinks. They probably still aren't playable (they have too many restrictions on their behavior-what an irony), but they should come off as something a enterprising ST could <i>make </i>playable, or even better, something a player of one of the Possessed might play on and off when one takes control. Yes, this crowds into Demon: the Descent, but then again they're both called demons; the Unchained should come off as being able to emphasize with the Infernal PoV very easily. Make it clear that the damnation of the Inferno is very much a self-inflicted one; in Willard Farnham's view of Faust, the good doctor's consignment to Hell is what drew ol' Mephy to him in the first place, rather than the other way around. Conspirators, not manipulators. Give them positive traits, things their honeyed words are genuine about; Mr. White <i>does </i>want to bring murderers to justice, Seminaza <i>wants </i>to make his host strong, popular, and happy. That is their difference-a demon has <i>empathy, </i>and <i>empathy </i>implies <i>altruism.</i> They don't exercise that all that often, but you can't guarantee that the succubus is just feeding on a convenient source; she could honestly love her summoner, and nothing in the world will make her betray him...which is hazardous to the cunning sap that thinks her lust makes her fickle, and thus, will <i>always </i>chose her power and survival when push comes to shove.<br /> <br /> In short, make them more human, because humans are unpredictable; monstrous one day, angelic the next, usually both. Add that to raw power and the understanding that, in order to survive and grow, they must be monstrous more often...<br /> <br /> Also, there's a lovely little concept called retcon; it's easy to make the Lord of Lies ability have flaws in it rather than just an invincible mental shield-Descent does this with Unchained lies, they can control everything that says they might be pulling something out of their ass...but nothing else, which is why they need Subterfuge to tell <i>good </i>lies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T11:18:35-08:00","id":406847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/393536-inferno-2nd-edition?p=406368#post406368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, in reality, it does not. Yes, you can have very &quot;inteligent&quot; or &quot;higher&quot; Shadow spirits. thinking in quasi-humans way - but their <i>raison d'\u00eatre</i>? To be on the top of foodchain - even Luna, Firstborns or probably Gaia - they all do what they do from the same reasons like lowerest mote - to promote their Essence connected to their Influnaces. On the level they are they have many ( and I mean <b>many</b> ) aspects of reality as their Essence generation, so the thing like Luna is Widow, Mother, Fickle Woman, Queen of Night, Destroyer, Dreamer, Seer, Trickster or Shadow ( yes, also as the Shadow of Shadow Realm ), It's all true - but from the Shadow Realm ecology stand point - she only is this things only to generate and claim more Essence for her, even if she does not conciess about it. You do not tell me Lunes are more thing than living automata of spiritual service - they can have personality, even elobarate. But in the end, all spirits are &quot;animals&quot; competing over recourse of Essence, even if we talk about abstract choirs.</div> </div> </div> </div> Humans are animals who compete to be top of the food chain too. That's something we can more than relate to. Just because a dog is an animal with a different thought process doesn't make it alien. <br /> <br /> That's splitting hairs. Demons are the embodiment of human sins, agreed? That's as much of a 'shard' of the human soul as a Goetic being, or a fully sentient ghost. They're as much a slice of human soul as any of the others.<br /> <br /> The Inferno loves messing with humans just as much as the Hisil spirits, the goetic beings, the ghosts. Humans aren't naturally hateful or killers. That behavior has to be learned, and the Inferno goes out of its way to actively encourage it. That's little different that a blood spirit from the Hisil nudging a human to engage in murder so it can feed off the killing. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It depends on the beings you describe. Qashmal or God Machine - sure, their ae about Plan. But the Empyrean angels described in Inferno? They are about <i>Virtues</i> - they are abuot <i>rules</i> the humanity governec <i>itself</i>. If Hells demons are about overthrowing rules of society, the Empyrean angels are about fortifing them, overthrowing them on those that do not want them. Chaos and Order, only on human scale. </div> </div> </div> With all due respect, I think you're just flat out wrong. That bits about being alien beings and all about the plan came right from the Inferno's write up. Yes, some of the Empyrean angels focus on Virtues (to the point of driving people insane, let me point out). Others are dedicated to the Apocalypse, no mention of virtues driving them. Or other strange tasks unrelated to anything humans understand. <br /> <br /> Again and again, the nature of Empyrean are pointed out to be alien beings that drive you crazy. It makes constant references to angels, qashmallim (same name as the beings from Promethean), and the Cherubim and Seraphim (the only time that's really used in the WoD is to refer to Aether angelic beings). At this point, the qashmal and supernal beings are the only ones described in the WoD. So, its more than possible that these beings actually ARE the qashmallim and supernal beings, or maybe God-Machine angels even. <br /> <br /> Never once have they been described as relating to humans. Constantly the opposite. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There is desctinctive - Lust Spirit ( lower one ) is half conciuse on it's actions. It want, literally, to get ( others to ) fuck. He is animialisitc in this. He does not make very eleborate plans and, hell no, work with some &quot;rules&quot;, or even break them. He <i>does not see</i> &quot;the rules&quot;. Inferno demons are all about <i>breaking</i> the rules. They get humans have marriages. They get humanity have idea of love. Binding of souls and all that. And they <i>love</i> it. Beacuse when there are rules, there is <i>transgression</i>, &quot;sin&quot;. Lust Spirit overrides women and makes her in to animal frenzy when she will fuck with any man she can meet - it's not picky, it just need Essence. Lust Demon will go to her and husbands apartment, call the hubby to come earlier - only to invite him to the orgy she made in mean time. Demon her &quot;won&quot; twice - it shakes the foundation of marriage, the monogamy they oath in the wedding day. And if husband liked the orgy, but was reclusive on the start, demon also broke <i>his</i> rules.<br /> <br /> Like I said earlier - Shadow spirits are &quot;animals&quot; of spirit world. Demons are very much the &quot;humans&quot; of it. </div> </div> </div> Umm... high ranked spirits (2+) are capable of some very grand plans. I really think you are underestimating what the spirits are capable of. I also think that you're mistaken in what Lust represents - its both more and less than sexual desire. And that you you are equating breaking rules with sins - that's not quite how it works. Demons feed off evil acts, yes. But we've got a clear idea of what makes up an evil act - choice, extremity, causing harm, malice, and a lack of remorse. Your description of rule breaking doesn't match the definition of evil acts as Inferno describes them (page 27-28). At no point in your description of the events has a demon &quot;won&quot; anything. Neither was an evil act, the demon gets nothing. At best, its the opening salvo to try and corrupt them into performing evil acts, but at this point, power is expended, and none gained.<br /> <br /> Yes, dominions feed differently than shadow spirits - the former gains power off corruption and &quot;evil acts,&quot; while the latter feeds off animistic (not to be confused with animalistic) reflections. That's not in debate. The problem is that doesn't make them human. Remember - there are Infernal demons who are still Hisil spirits. They may be tainted by the inferno, but, by your own description, they are still &quot;animals.&quot; They still feed off Hisil essence.<br /> <br /> Demons gain empathy for humans. That doesn't make them human like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T11:34:35-08:00","id":406872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/393536-inferno-2nd-edition?p=406736#post406736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they wanted to add more new stuff, there is actually quite a bit of room left (as others have mentioned before):</div> </div> </div> </div> Even more mechanics! Yay! No setting updates! <br /> <br /> While I think that a mechanics update would be nice, that's not exactly difficult. <br /> <br /> Chapter 1 - bring the dominions and whisperers into line with the regular spirit rules for manifestation and the like. Update a few of the Numina. Vices unimportant - generally speaking, the only real mechanical effect is what influence it can take, so there's no need to have any description about them. No need for dealing with how Integrity works. Demons never interacted with Morality, so there's no reason for Integrity to change it.<br /> <br /> Chapter 2 - updates to powers granted. Research rolls and summoning remain the same. Benefits from pacts could use updating, but that's not hard, bringing them in line with current supernatural merits for mortals.<br /> <br /> Chapter 3 - new rules for the Possessed. You can just keep the seven sins as the branches and just update the Vestments; treat the sins as abstract categories instead of firm ones. Update experience chart. Some beats for making others commit evil acts, maybe, feed the demon. Everything else is fine. Empyrean needs no new words, since we don't even know if they exist as a separate entity from God Machine angels, Principle qashmallim, or Supernal seraphim/cherubim. <br /> <br /> Chapter 4 - Example monsters are examples. L'enfant diablique are &quot;evil lucifuge&quot; served as part of Hunter's line. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/393536-inferno-2nd-edition?p=406802#post406802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quite. That's why I advocate a different idea; focus on the demons and not the people who pact with them. Show what it's like to be Mephistopheles from his side of the pentagram, how a demon thinks. They probably still aren't playable (they have too many restrictions on their behavior-what an irony), but they should come off as something a enterprising ST could <i>make </i>playable, or even better, something a player of one of the Possessed might play on and off when one takes control. Yes, this crowds into Demon: the Descent, but then again they're both called demons; the Unchained should come off as being able to emphasize with the Infernal PoV very easily. Make it clear that the damnation of the Inferno is very much a self-inflicted one; in Willard Farnham's view of Faust, the good doctor's consignment to Hell is what drew ol' Mephy to him in the first place, rather than the other way around. Conspirators, not manipulators. Give them positive traits, things their honeyed words are genuine about; Mr. White <i>does </i>want to bring murderers to justice, Seminaza <i>wants </i>to make his host strong, popular, and happy. That is their difference-a demon has <i>empathy, </i>and <i>empathy </i>implies <i>altruism.</i> They don't exercise that all that often, but you can't guarantee that the succubus is just feeding on a convenient source; she could honestly love her summoner, and nothing in the world will make her betray him...which is hazardous to the cunning sap that thinks her lust makes her fickle, and thus, will <i>always </i>chose her power and survival when push comes to shove.</div> </div> </div> </div> Crowds into? I think the phrase you're looking for is &quot;trying to reinvent the wheel.&quot; You are describing Descent when you're talking about turning Inferno into that, and completely and utterly destroying the whole point of Inferno being the essence of evil and feeding on evil acts. That is pretty much the sole definition of the Inferno we do have here. Pure evil.<br /> <br /> <br /> Oh, and no. Empathy does not imply altruism. You are confusing empathy with sympathy. Empathy just means you can understand and relate to the feelings of others. It doesn't mean that you will be ruled or guided by said emotions at any point.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, there's a lovely little concept called retcon; it's easy to make the Lord of Lies ability have flaws in it rather than just an invincible mental shield-Descent does this with Unchained lies, they can control everything that says they might be pulling something out of their ass...but nothing else, which is why they need Subterfuge to tell <i>good </i>lies. </div> </div> </div> I suggest you read Flowers of Hell for the limitations of the Unchained lying ability, and the associated rolls needed. Possessed don't have the Lord of Lies ability, and spirits can't roll subterfuge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 02-15-2015, 03:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T13:49:41-08:00","id":406957,"title":"","content":"Talking abour Inferno....Does anyone remember <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/119411-fiend-the-transaction-a-storytelling-game-of-temptation\">this post</a>? I would love to see its mechanics updated and adapted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T17:59:39-08:00","id":407200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/393536-inferno-2nd-edition?p=406498#post406498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe the rules of interaction? Spirits need the Resonance to build up. The Demons should interact when &quot;Sins&quot; (Transgressions ) of their Malepraxies come to being. If Spirit of Lust comes when people make a Night Club in reality the Dark Room to randomly fuck with each other - the Demon of List comes when perfect marriage is destroyed by the act of infidelity, killing the wife in perverted way. Spirits need build up, Hell's Demons need atrocities. I think it would change all &quot;we need this and those Conditions&quot; mechanics enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I wrote my own rough conversion of the Dominion I took this into account and you're right that this is the best way to create a difference in the two entities. At this point, however, one has to focus on the concept of <i>transgression</i> as the route of sin and so it becomes less attached to the modern vice system and instead you go back to that old 7 Deadly Sins rule but instead of relating it to the willpower regenerating action of nearby humans you base it solely on that transgression.<br /> <br /> Example: Before the Lust Demon would gain willpower and essence if anyone gave in to its Malapraxis because their vice was lust. Since, unless a character chooses one of the Seven Deadly Sins as their vice, this is far more unlikely to come up, I uncoupled it from the system of a character vice. Instead, the demon regains willpower and essence if anyone engages in the sinful practice of its Malapraxis period, regardless of their beliefs, so long as the action itself is both transgressing and destructive in some way.<br /> <br /> To further this idea I decided that 'Malus Loci' should be their dependent condition. Where a Spirit is 'Resonant' with anything within its nature a Demon is not. It feeds on malice and transgression so anywhere where such things occurred become 'Malus Loci'.<br /> <br /> Continuing the example of the Lust Demon he can only regain essence and prevent essence bleed while haunting, for example, the master bedroom of a married couple's house because the husband brought his mistress home and desecrated their bed with the transgression. It is both a transgression of virtue, so sin, and is destructive behaviour that if found out about would damage his marriage.<br /> <br /> However, with all of that said, there still is an inherent problem. Spirits are just so damn broad and undefined. A Spirit of Lust, one could argue, would only resonate with transgressive behaviour because it isn't a Spirit of Sex or a Spirit of Revelry, it is a Spirit of Lust which carries with it the connotation of transgression already. Essentially, a Spirit of Lust is an <i>evil spirit</i> already or put another way: <i>a spirit of lust is already a demon.</i><br /> <br /> So while in the short-term this serves for those of us who want to use a Demon in a certain way and separate them from Spirits an easy argument can be made that it's still the same thing and that all we're doing is renaming the Resonant condition and Nature of a more specifically aligned spirit to &quot;Malus Loci&quot; and &quot;Malapraxis&quot;.<br /> <br /> At current, in their broad mechanical nature, the three Ephemeral Creature types serve most (if not all) purposes one could need for a monster in <i>any</i> chronicle. That is: A Ghost is a personality that follows a personality's motivation. A Spirit is a conceptual entity that feeds on a certain concept and encourages that concept. An Angel is a ordered being that follows a specific task, even if that task is nonsense. This is why I feel as if for a Dominion to be <i>truly</i> distinct as an entity it would have to be more akin to the Strix and possess its own rules entirely and be detached from the concept of being an Ephemeral Creature.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/393536-inferno-2nd-edition?p=406802#post406802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Quite. That's why I advocate a different idea; focus on the demons and not the people who pact with them. Show what it's like to be Mephistopheles from his side of the pentagram, how a demon thinks. They probably still aren't playable (they have too many restrictions on their behavior-what an irony), but they should come off as something a enterprising ST could <i>make </i>playable, or even better, something a player of one of the Possessed might play on and off when one takes control. Yes, this crowds into Demon: the Descent, but then again they're both called demons; the Unchained should come off as being able to emphasize with the Infernal PoV very easily. Make it clear that the damnation of the Inferno is very much a self-inflicted one; in Willard Farnham's view of Faust, the good doctor's consignment to Hell is what drew ol' Mephy to him in the first place, rather than the other way around. Conspirators, not manipulators. Give them positive traits, things their honeyed words are genuine about; Mr. White <i>does </i>want to bring murderers to justice, Seminaza <i>wants </i>to make his host strong, popular, and happy. That is their difference-a demon has <i>empathy, </i>and <i>empathy </i>implies <i>altruism.</i> They don't exercise that all that often, but you can't guarantee that the succubus is just feeding on a convenient source; she could honestly love her summoner, and nothing in the world will make her betray him...which is hazardous to the cunning sap that thinks her lust makes her fickle, and thus, will <i>always </i>chose her power and survival when push comes to shove.<br /> <br /> In short, make them more human, because humans are unpredictable; monstrous one day, angelic the next, usually both. Add that to raw power and the understanding that, in order to survive and grow, they must be monstrous more often...<br /> <br /> Also, there's a lovely little concept called retcon; it's easy to make the Lord of Lies ability have flaws in it rather than just an invincible mental shield-Descent does this with Unchained lies, they can control everything that says they might be pulling something out of their ass...but nothing else, which is why they need Subterfuge to tell <i>good </i>lies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like you just described to me the True Fae from Changeling the Lost. These are entities fueled by their passions, ordinary or bizarre, that are decoupled from the mundane concepts of &quot;good and evil&quot; and any dual nature that notion represents. Fae do what they want or do what they do, for whatever reason. The rules in this regard are even called &quot;Ruled by their Passions&quot; on several True Fae stat block. They are <i>often</i> sinister, but not <i>always. </i>Sometimes True Fae just want a friend and sometimes they find a child willing to be that friend and their leading them into Arcadia never to return is, quite frankly, only caused due to both the child and the True Fae's inability to understand the concept of consequences.<br /> <br /> Inferno's core character, as MCN says, kinda <i>have</i> to be <i>evil. Without compromise.</i> They can trick you into <i>thinking</i> they aren't evil, but they are as evil as they come.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T02:19:54-08:00","id":407528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DesolateDolly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/393536-inferno-2nd-edition?p=407200#post407200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like you just described to me the True Fae from Changeling the Lost. These are entities fueled by their passions, ordinary or bizarre, that are decoupled from the mundane concepts of &quot;good and evil&quot; and any dual nature that notion represents. Fae do what they want or do what they do, for whatever reason. The rules in this regard are even called &quot;Ruled by their Passions&quot; on several True Fae stat block. They are <i>often</i> sinister, but not <i>always. </i>Sometimes True Fae just want a friend and sometimes they find a child willing to be that friend and their leading them into Arcadia never to return is, quite frankly, only caused due to both the child and the True Fae's inability to understand the concept of consequences</div> </div> </div> </div>In short, the True Fae act like children. Over powered children with powers that would make a Mary Sue drool but children none the less. They act wild and have the temper of a twister at times but overall childish. Like all childhood, this comes at a time of somewhat self centeredness but also lessons about learning about others. True Fae are perpetually on the verge of learning what the Other is and that one can exist without partaking in conflict but never quite reaching the goal.<br /> <br /> This is reflected via the Virtue and Vice being inverse. The True Fae does can act somewhat kind and whatnot (and perhaps do the best to exercise it in relation to their title) but if their Vice is triggered... Well, may God help you.<br /> <br /> Infernal Demons on the other hand, are much more evil. While the True Fae can and does practice it's virtue from time to time, it's usually an extension of their childish outlook. They didn't <i>mean </i>hurt the little doggie. They just wanted to pet it but then it started to bite them and they hate it when it bites so they just gave it a sharp twist to make it be quiet. But now the doggie is quiet all the time and that's boring. Even after they gave it food and water and some friends to play with but now it just lays there. They'll just have to go get another one.<br /> <br /> Infernal Demon, nah, the fucker gave you knew <i>exactly</i> what he was doing when he did the thing. He tied you to a chair, sliced off your eye lids, and fucking made you watch as he tormented you with it's cries. He laughed as adrenaline flooded your system and you broke out of the chair only to find a box with a recording of the dog's screams and the Demon's Testament constructed out of it's skins. And you? The first one to scream it's name so loud that others will hear, others that may yet summon it. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T18:56:24-08:00","id":408450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/393536-inferno-2nd-edition?p=406957#post406957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Talking abour Inferno....Does anyone remember <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/119411-fiend-the-transaction-a-storytelling-game-of-temptation\">this post</a>? I would love to see its mechanics updated and adapted.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I honestly dropped that because I wasn't getting much feedback; all of its mechanics are GMC compatible, though I will have to give them a firm shake-n-bake to make them not <i>awful</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> That is to say, I'll approach them and make them workable, if you want me to. (I also wrote up Ephemeral Being rules for Inferno Demons <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/318864-more-ephemeral-entity-types#post318864\">here</a>.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". 02-16-2015, 10:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T12:50:22-08:00","id":409237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>EDIT:</b> That is to say, I'll approach them and make them workable, if you want me to </div> </div> </div><br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/202DvmQ.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T18:10:14-08:00","id":413526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/393536-inferno-2nd-edition?p=408450#post408450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know, I honestly dropped that because I wasn't getting much feedback; all of its mechanics are GMC compatible, though I will have to give them a firm shake-n-bake to make them not <i>awful</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> That is to say, I'll approach them and make them workable, if you want me to. (I also wrote up Ephemeral Being rules for Inferno Demons <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/318864-more-ephemeral-entity-types#post318864&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.)</div> </div> </div> </div>That's really Cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T06:36:16-08:00","id":414006,"title":"","content":"I would like rules to clarify the effects of trading dots of willpower for power, like making the Fiend less human (or at least more disturbing).<br /> Also, the pacts mechanics should be more freeform, like a semi-open magic system based on effects associated with cardinal sins.,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T11:51:01-07:00","id":436021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/393536-inferno-2nd-edition?p=404065#post404065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bear in mind that if we get a 2e-esque Inferno, it\u2019s going to be using 2e-esque Vices, which aren\u2019t so much about \u201cdoing evil things\u201d as \u201ctaking the easy way out\u201d: <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">A character's Vice, on the other hand, is a source of short-term comfort and a distraction from the world. Vice should be the easy way out, the sand he buries his head in, like a bully lashing out to avoid his own fear or an alcoholic drinking to forget.</span> Put another way, your Vice is the mechanism you use to cope with the problems in your life without actually dealing with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the best argument for ditching the big seven as far as sings go, because it parallels the weak and shallow nature of Inferno demons. (It does however entail a big overhaul for Possessed's powers).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/393536-inferno-2nd-edition?p=406872#post406872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chapter 1 - bring the dominions and whisperers into line with the regular spirit rules for manifestation and the like. Update a few of the Numina. Vices unimportant - generally speaking, the only real mechanical effect is what influence it can take, so there's no need to have any description about them. No need for dealing with how Integrity works. Demons never interacted with Morality, so there's no reason for Integrity to change it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Chapter 2 - updates to powers granted. Research rolls and summoning remain the same. Benefits from pacts could use updating, but that's not hard, bringing them in line with current supernatural merits for mortals. </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Chapter 3 - new rules for the Possessed. You can just keep the seven sins as the branches and just update the Vestments; treat the sins as abstract categories instead of firm ones. Update experience chart. Some beats for making others commit evil acts, maybe, feed the demon. Everything else is fine. </div> </div> </div>If the possible sin bases for demons is widened, the powers need to be too; maybe design the powers so they can have an &quot;on/for&quot; slotted into them according to a demon/Possessed's particular sins. Or maybe have it as a setting element that the Possessed <i>do</i> tend to exemplify a narrower set of sins than demons in general, and that's why those became more generally recognised.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Chapter 4 - Example monsters are examples. L'enfant diablique are &quot;evil lucifuge&quot; served as part of Hunter's line. </div> </div> </div>I'd break this in half. Example demons, and example cults and worshippers. Les Enfants can be part of the latter - so can the Belial's Brood and Bale Hounds excised from the second editions of Vampire and Werewolf - perhaps along with changeling and sineater analogues.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T15:49:43-07:00","id":633897,"title":"","content":"There's some place where the devs show us what is being planned?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T02:53:47-07:00","id":634394,"title":"","content":"In general or about a posible 2nd edition version of Inferno?<br /> <br /> In general you have the Onix Path blogs and the social media accounts.<br /> <br /> As for Inferno, is just wishful thinking on our part, no official anouncement that it is even being considered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T03:02:11-07:00","id":634409,"title":"","content":"Isn't the whole argument about infernals being the same mechanically speaking as other existing creatures, the same as arguing to stop using all kinds of different mechanics and simply start using the Hunter Vigil dread powers for all opponents regardless of splat book mechanics? It would certainly make it a lot easier for story tellers to use other monsters without the need to buy a large amount of books <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Then you can make one design book about tempters, whether that is True Fae, the God Machine, Ghosts or Devil-like entities and how to use them in various game lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T07:32:56-07:00","id":634583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/393536-inferno-2nd-edition?p=633897#post633897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's some place where the devs show us what is being planned?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/category/news/monday-meeting/\" target=\"_blank\">The Monday Meetings.</a><br /> <br /> And the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/schedule/\" target=\"_blank\">current project page</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T15:11:59-07:00","id":636300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/393536-inferno-2nd-edition?p=634583#post634583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/category/news/monday-meeting/\" target=\"_blank\">The Monday Meetings.</a><br /> <br /> And the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/schedule/\" target=\"_blank\">current project page</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the info, but I was talking about an open discussion between players and developers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/393536-inferno-2nd-edition?p=634394#post634394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In general or about a posible 2nd edition version of Inferno?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes please.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/393536-inferno-2nd-edition?p=634394#post634394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Inferno, is just wishful thinking on our part, no official anouncement that it is even being considered.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aaaah. T_T","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T17:57:47-07:00","id":1249240,"title":"","content":"In addition to the Goetic Demons and the derivatives of the Christian tradition we have two more types of demons.<br /> <br /> The Specimens of East Asian Culture, whether in Buddhism, Shintoism or contrary to the Celestial Hierarchy, can be classified as another beast (as the Fairies and Vampires were dissociated from the Demons).<br /> <br /> And the Zoroastrian Demons, these can not be and they have nothing associated with falling into them. They are the fruits of evil and bring this in their essence to destroy order and creation.<br /> <br /> I think that Hell Second Edition should deal with Ahriman as more than a powerful Goetic spirit. And it treats it as its own, as it is treated in its culture.<br /> <br /> I even think like Mummy has an Egyptian base. Inferno should have Persian base.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T20:02:20-07:00","id":1249255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Linus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/393536-inferno-2nd-edition?p=1249240#post1249240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In addition to the Goetic Demons and the derivatives of the Christian tradition we have two more types of demons.<br /> <br /> The Specimens of East Asian Culture, whether in Buddhism, Shintoism or contrary to the Celestial Hierarchy, can be classified as another beast (as the Fairies and Vampires were dissociated from the Demons).<br /> <br /> And the Zoroastrian Demons, these can not be and they have nothing associated with falling into them. They are the fruits of evil and bring this in their essence to destroy order and creation.<br /> <br /> I think that Hell Second Edition should deal with Ahriman as more than a powerful Goetic spirit. And it treats it as its own, as it is treated in its culture.<br /> <br /> I even think like Mummy has an Egyptian base. Inferno should have Persian base.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, this post was 3 years old.<br /> <br /> It is generally implied that many of these are the same entities. Lucifuge and the Otodo are basically being the Christian/Shinto equivalent of one another, with a similar power set (albeit with a different focus). The Inferno demons didn't really have any association with the God Machine Demons, who where the more classical fire an' brimstone type. They arn't really necessarily tied to the concept of &quot;falling&quot;, as they arn't God Machine demons. Inferno even has a sidebar dealing with some of this,&quot;Multicultural Demonology&quot;, for several explanations of what the demons are/say they are, with one option being that they appear based on the dominant mythology (to the point where an atheist would see them as a mental illness, rather than the satanic form a Christian would see them as).<br /> <br /> Then there is the fact that some abilities work on Demons tend to work on the entire group. There isn't really much to gain from separating demons into a bunch of different things, any more than there is to split apart Vampires from their various local interpretation. Its confusing enough as it is anyway :P<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T11:00:12-07:00","id":1249491,"title":"","content":"The subject is still very current. Should I have created a new topic?<br /> <br /> Universalizing something requires care for the interpretation of what is not circumscribed and therefore the &quot;universalism&quot; is forced. The Crone Circle is an example of a pseudo-universalism that only interprets the old ones about a twentieth-century neo-paganism that has nothing to do with Ancient Polytheistic traditions, even because these traditions are distinct enough for eg Politeismo Indo-European differentiate itself more from the Meso-American than Christianity. And Crone's Ethos is just poor modern neo-age mischief, not something present in ancient traditions. The same thing happened with the Old Hell that placed all the legends within a modern Goetia interpretation shifting from its original meanings and reducing all the demons to representations of the collective psyche like figures and tulpas.<br /> <br /> On other creatures, it is not because they are beings of other cultures, but because Demons are confused with beings that already have games, like powerful and terrible spirits, beings thresholds, true faes and vampires. The European Fairies, Arabian Geniuses and Japanese Oni for example fit into Faes. Many Demons from Eastern Europe and Japan are clearly spirits.<br /> <br /> As the Descent absorbs well the Christian Demons, even the Pernostics, but mainly the Platonic and Gnostic ones.<br /> <br /> The Mesoamerican and East Asian mythologies each fit a type of creature-game of their own to derive from the Demon parameter. And each of these is close to its neighbors enough to have a cultural environment that can be fully represented, as it does with the West and with differences as large as one Western country to another. Soon a couple of new lines of games solve this problem.<br /> <br /> The Goetic beings already exist in Mago, Inferno ends up being even a redundant book.<br /> <br /> There are only things Lovecraftianas that should be a Blue Book itself (like the Contagion). And the Original Demons, who are Zoroastrians.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T13:30:20-07:00","id":1249518,"title":"","content":"It probably wouldn't have hurt, but I have no idea what the actual policy is :P<br /> <br /> &quot;Universalism&quot; is absolutely necessary in some form, or there would be far too many books and &quot;spare-change&quot; to keep track of. A necromancer reviving the dead and messing around with ghosts and an mage mucking around with time are both distinctive concepts from different cultures, but they both fit under the umbrella for &quot;magic user&quot; letting them both be mages. We don't need a splat just for &quot;Necromancers&quot; and a splat for &quot;Time Witches&quot;, or everything gets cut into such small parts that the world gets even more cluttered than it already is.<br /> <br /> It can be because they are beings of other cultures, by that sidebar's reckoning, and not that they are just confused for them. It explicitly says that the GM can make it so that Taoism is right, and that demons made up the other religions for lolz. The thing is that the difference between &quot;evil spirits&quot; and &quot;inferno demons&quot; is fuzzy even from a meta perspective. Back to my example, the Otodo would suggest that Oni are closer to the demons that made the Lucifuge, which may or may not be the Inferno demons. Mortal Remains puts them under the same umbrella, calling the Inferno type &quot;Lesser demons&quot; (and namedropping Whispers) while the God-Machine demons are the &quot;Greater Demons&quot;, with &quot;anti-demon&quot; powers that the Lucifuge has working on both of them equally. Inferno has the L' Enfant Diabolique, who's close approximation of the Lucifuge suggest that they would be born of Inferno style demons. The only real way to tell a particularly mean spirit from a demon is to do something that works on one and not the other, and it isn't like we get a lot of examples of that happening in the fluff. Then there is the &quot;Demons&quot; that the Knights of Saint George use, which may or may not be related to either or both.<br /> <br /> 2E Goetia arn't really close to Inferno or Christian Demons, in form or function, as &quot;entities of pure thought or concept&quot; who don't usually possess people or do particularly nasty things for no other reason than they are evil beings. They don't really overlap much, aside from being called demon occasionally.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-30T00:23:17-07:00","id":1315396,"title":"","content":"Thing I wish it was Inferno 2.0<br /> <br /> I very much hope that they will abandon the Goethian approach of the first edition by a Zoroastrian approach in that second. And I expect the two in X to be what their function for Ahriman (based on the 6 Persian archetypes - 1 - Akoman - Corruptors, Seducers, Tempters 2 - Indar - Dark Lords, Proud Rulers, punish their enemies and reward their devotees. &quot;righteous&quot; 3 - Nanghait - Punishers and Torturers 4 - Sawar - They are not Corruptors and Corrupt and Vicious 5 - Tauriz - Agents of Conflict and Destruction 6 - Zariz - Cheaters and Entities with opposing natures or contradictory purposes and will contradictory to its purpose) and the Y in what is this demon (1 - Angels, Djins and Fallen Gods - like the Christian and Muslim version 2 - Demons Reborn as such by Carma - like the Buddhist, Hindu and Taoist versions. - Creation of Ahriman 4 - Destructive Natural Spirits such as Chagas the Negative Entities of Shinto 5 - Dark Gods - Paganism 6 - Deviant Gods - like the rulers of Xibalba 7 - Contaminated Spirits and Supernatural Beings very evil and mighty ones that were destroyed. 8 - Unclaimed Human Souls that fell there and ascended - Spiritist Dragons. 9. Forgotten Gods. 10 - Others, including Goethias things).<br /> <br /> Zoroastrism is unfortunately little used in fiction but Vertigo had done an excellent job of it as the basis for other metaphysics within them. As of the Original Demons criticizing the Fallen Angels, &quot;these angels came and think that they rule here, but they do not know that we are much older than the creator of their rebel leader.&quot;<br /> <br /> Ahriman is not the opposite pole to God Machine. A Great Entity of the Dark Mother Level, The Divine Fire, and the Machine God certainly, but something even older than these. Older than anything and indifferent to other great entities but treated by them as Contagion is. And seen as something external.<br /> <br /> It would be interesting until such a thing was dead (as Kamen Rider Black worked, waiting for a successor who will never come). But I do not know if hell would not get too big, just like the contagion and end up becoming a crossover supplement. Against the Created and Corrupted by the Forgotten God. This would refer to the God of Yellow too, where Darkness and Evil precede everything, not all evil came from it, but it was the first thing that arose, a reversal of Christianity in which Sin is disobedience and denial of Light that the Natural State. Here we would have the Darkness is the Natural State, the light is a rare event (which tends to create in new darkness distinct from primordial darkness and averse to it as much as light itself).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}